HELP = r"""asksoul {version}: ask your Grok Bot main bot from this terminal.

Give your bot this repo and let it set up; SETUP.md walks it through. This
help is the CLI reference.

CLI
---

Usage:
  asksoul [-s ID] [-w WHO] [-t SEC] [--wait SEC] [--json] [--] MESSAGE
  asksoul wait ID [--wait SEC]    read the next answer, say nothing
  asksoul close ID                end the conversation
  asksoul ls                      open conversations (header row first)
  asksoul tui [-s ID] [-w WHO] [-t SEC] [--wait SEC]
                                  interactive chat in this terminal
  asksoul init [options]          write the config file
  asksoul -h | --version

The default command says MESSAGE and prints {bot}'s answer. A MESSAGE that
is literally ls, wait, close, tui or init goes after --:  asksoul -- ls

Three delivery layers, weakest first:
  1. ack      "# ack (by {bot})" / "DELIVERY ack"
              {bot} received your line.
  2. relayed  "# relayed: <bot> (by {bot})" / "DELIVERY relayed"
              handed to a teammate bot; not proof that bot read it.
  3. [bot]    "[<name>] ..."   the bot itself answered.
If --wait ends with no ack the status is "unconfirmed". With --json the same
status is also one line of JSON: {"delivery":"ack"|"relayed"|"unconfirmed"}.

Exit codes (take the code from the call itself, not from a pipe):
  0  got an answer (session still open), or close <ID> done
  1  usage / no open session / Ctrl-C (the conversation goes on)
  2  could not reach the bot (webhook failed); not delivered, not kept
  3  conversation ended by -t silence
  4  fatal setup (config / bind / allowlist / crypto)
  5  ended after 3 consecutive bad MACs (start a new session)
  6  a relayed arrived: done, never resend; wait <ID> may still read a line
  7  the bot closed the conversation
  8  --wait ran out with nothing yet; wait <ID> keeps waiting
  9  only an ack arrived; wait <ID> keeps waiting

Conversations. -s ID names one session. Without -s a fresh ID is printed on
stderr: "asksoul: session <ID> (continue with -s <ID>)". Each call says one
line and returns after one turn; the conversation stays open until
close <ID>, or until -t seconds pass with nothing said by either side.

stdout:
  [{bot}] <text>                          the bot said this
  [{bot}, queued 2026-10-09 21:15 +08:00] <text>   said earlier, delivered late
  # ack (by <from>)                       <from> received your line
  # relayed: <bot> (by {bot})             handed to a teammate bot
  DELIVERY ack|relayed|unconfirmed        machine-readable status
stderr carries diagnostics only.

Options:
  -h, --help            this text
  -w, --who WHO         self-name for this run
  -t, --timeout SEC     idle seconds before the conversation ends (default
                        300, 1..86400); set when the session opens
  -s, --session ID      1..128 of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ : -, starting with a
                        letter or digit
      --wait SEC        this call waits at most SEC seconds for an answer
                        (default 300, 1..86400); the conversation stays open
      --json            also print one delivery JSON line

The bot is woken by the webhook; a cold start often needs a minute or more.
Set --wait / -t in minutes, not a few seconds. If the bot asks something,
answer with -s <ID>. Close when the exchange is done, not after the first
line.

TUI
---

  asksoul tui [-s ID] [-w WHO] [-t SEC] [--wait SEC]

A small curses chat, stdlib only: one status line (session, who, idle), a
scrollable transcript and a 1-3 line input. No MESSAGE argument: the session
opens on the first Enter and that line is its first message. TUI is a
continuous conversation: {bot} answers with ask (or send without close) and
must not close after each turn — only on /close, idle timeout, or an explicit
end.
Without -s a fresh id is made and printed once on stderr; -w / -t / --wait
work as above (-w and -t only when the TUI opens the session). Inbound frames
appear while idle. msg and relayed use the same "[from] ..." / "# relayed:
..." lines as stdout; status frames are "# status: ..."; the local echo is
"[you] ...".
Keys: Enter sends; Backspace edits; Esc clears the draft; PgUp/PgDn scroll
the transcript (Up/Down one line); Ctrl-L redraws. Pasted text keeps embedded
newlines in one draft; Enter outside a paste still sends. Ctrl-C cancels a
wait and leaves the session open; Ctrl-C while idle closes the session and
exits 0. A non-TTY run prints "asksoul tui needs a TTY" and exits 2.
Slash commands (Enter):
  /help            short help in the transcript
  /clear           clear the transcript view (the session stays open)
  /wait            wait for the next inbound message, send nothing
  /close, /quit    close the session and exit
  other /...       shown locally; never sent as a message

Setup
-----

Config: ~/.config/asksoul/config.toml (mode 0600). `asksoul init` writes it,
interactively or with flags:
  asksoul init --webhook-url URL --bot-name NAME --accept HOST[,HOST...] \
      --secret-cmd 'security find-generic-password -s asksoul -w'
  asksoul init --webhook-url URL --secret-stdin   # secret from stdin to a file
  asksoul init --non-interactive --webhook-url URL # no prompts

Config keys (flat TOML):
  bot_name          main bot name in output (default "Soul")
  webhook_url       webhook URL from the routine trigger (required)
  accept            list/comma list of IPs or hostnames allowed to dial back
  accept_ssh_host   optional ssh config Host whose HostName is allowed
  bind              local IPv4 to listen on (default: `tailscale ip -4`)
  secret_cmd        shell command whose stdout is the webhook secret
  secret_file       file containing the secret (must be mode 0600)
  who, source       optional caller identity
  transport         optional free-form label (default "tcp-tailnet")

Environment overrides: ASKSOUL_CONFIG, ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_URL,
ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET, ASKSOUL_BOT_NAME, ASKSOUL_ACCEPT, ASKSOUL_BIND,
ASKSOUL_ACCEPT_SSH_HOST, ASKSOUL_SECRET_CMD, ASKSOUL_SECRET_FILE,
ASKSOUL_WHO, ASKSOUL_SOURCE, ASKSOUL_TAILSCALE.
Secret precedence: ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET > secret_cmd > secret_file.
The config holds no secret unless you choose secret_file. Never paste the
webhook secret into chat.

Test hook: ASKSOUL_NO_WEBHOOK=1 skips the POST and prints the dial-back
host/port/key_b64/session_id as one JSON line on stderr. It is for local
protocol tests only.

How it works
------------

Opening a session binds a TCP listener on the configured bind address and an
ephemeral port with a fresh 32-byte key, POSTs the webhook, and starts a
background session process (no terminal). Each asksoul call talks to that
process and returns after one turn. If no bot is connected when a -s line
arrives, the process re-POSTs the webhook for the same session_id and the bot
dials in again. Every webhook POST retries network errors, 429 and 5xx up to
3 times, then the call exits 2.

The listener accepts only peers on the accept allowlist. One bot connection
at a time; sequential reconnects are fine. A bot that disconnects without
close does not end the session.

Protocol
--------

Webhook payload:
  {"source":...,"who":...,"sender_type":"user-cli"|"user-tui",
   "intent":"asksoul","message":...,"session_id":...,
   "reply":{"required":true,"mode":"session","transport":"tcp-tailnet",
            "host":...,"port":...,"timeout_sec":...,
            "crypto":{"alg":"hmac-sha256-v1","key_b64":...},
            "accept":"session","note":...}}

The bot dials reply.host:reply.port and sends line-delimited JSON frames:
  {"v":1,"alg":"hmac-sha256-v1","kind":...,"session_id":...,
   "from":...,"mac_b64":...,"body_b64":...}
MAC (bytes): body; or from + "\n" + body; with queued_at:
from + "\0" + queued_at + "\n" + body. Kinds: status (stderr only), msg
(text), relayed (hand-off receipt), close (end the session), ack (automatic
first frame on every dial, before anything else). Three consecutive bad
MACs end the session (exit 5). Full reference: docs/protocol.md.

The bot-side helper is `asksoul-talk` on PATH (installed with this repo's
bot/asksoul-talk).
"""


USAGE = (
    'asksoul [-s ID] [-w WHO] [-t SEC] [--wait SEC] [--] MESSAGE\n'
    '                  talk (the default)\n'
    'asksoul wait ID [--wait SEC]   next turn, send nothing\n'
    'asksoul close ID               end the session\n'
    'asksoul ls                     open sessions (header row first)\n'
    'asksoul tui [-s ID] [-w WHO] [-t SEC] [--wait SEC]\n'
    '                  interactive chat in this terminal\n'
    'asksoul init [options]         write the config file\n'
    'asksoul -h                     this text'
)


class UsageError(Exception):
    pass


class SetupError(Exception):
    pass


class WebhookError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, detail: str, attempts: int = 1) -> None:
        super().__init__(detail)
        self.detail = detail
        self.attempts = attempts


class _NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
    def redirect_request(self, req, fp, code, msg, headers, newurl):  # type: ignore[no-untyped-def]
        return None


_OPENER = urllib.request.build_opener(_NoRedirect)


def eprint(msg: str) -> None:
    sys.stderr.write(f"asksoul: {msg}\n")
    try:
        sys.stderr.flush()
    except OSError:
        pass


def _split_comment(line: str) -> str:
    """Strip a # comment that is outside quotes."""
    out: list[str] = []
    quote: Optional[str] = None
    escaped = False
    for ch in line:
        if escaped:
            out.append(ch)
            escaped = False
            continue
        if quote == '"' and ch == "\\":
            out.append(ch)
            escaped = True
            continue
        if quote is not None:
            out.append(ch)
            if ch == quote:
                quote = None
            continue
        if ch in ("'", '"'):
            quote = ch
            out.append(ch)
            continue
        if ch == "#":
            break
        out.append(ch)
    return "".join(out).strip()


def _split_array(text: str) -> list[str]:
    items: list[str] = []
    depth = 0
    quote: Optional[str] = None
    escaped = False
    start = 0
    for index, ch in enumerate(text):
        if escaped:
            escaped = False
            continue
        if quote == '"' and ch == "\\":
            escaped = True
            continue
        if quote is not None:
            if ch == quote:
                quote = None
            continue
        if ch in ("'", '"'):
            quote = ch
        elif ch == "[":
            depth += 1
        elif ch == "]":
            depth -= 1
        elif ch == "," and depth == 0:
            items.append(text[start:index].strip())
            start = index + 1
    tail = text[start:].strip()
    if tail:
        items.append(tail)
    return [item for item in items if item]


def _parse_toml_value(raw: str) -> Any:
    raw = raw.strip()
    if raw.startswith('"'):
        try:
            return json.loads(raw)
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            return raw.strip('"')
    if raw.startswith("'"):
        return raw[1:-1] if raw.endswith("'") else raw[1:]
    if raw.startswith("[") and raw.endswith("]"):
        return [_parse_toml_value(item) for item in _split_array(raw[1:-1])]
    lowered = raw.lower()
    if lowered == "true":
        return True
    if lowered == "false":
        return False
    if re.fullmatch(r"[+-]?\d+", raw):
        try:
            return int(raw)
        except ValueError:
            pass
    if re.fullmatch(r"[+-]?\d+\.\d+", raw):
        try:
            return float(raw)
        except ValueError:
            pass
    return raw


def _parse_flat_toml(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The Python 3.9/3.10 fallback: flat key = value, string arrays allowed.

    Sections are flattened to dotted keys; nested tables are not otherwise
    interpreted. The config this tool writes is flat.
    """
    data: dict[str, Any] = {}
    section = ""
    for raw in text.splitlines():
        line = _split_comment(raw)
        if not line:
            continue
        if line.startswith("[") and line.endswith("]"):
            section = line[1:-1].strip()
            continue
        if "=" not in line:
            raise UsageError(f"config line is not key = value: {raw.strip()!r}")
        key, value = line.split("=", 1)
        key = key.strip()
        if not key:
            raise UsageError(f"config line has an empty key: {raw.strip()!r}")
        full = f"{section}.{key}" if section else key
        data[full] = _parse_toml_value(value)
    return data


def parse_toml(text: str) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Parse config.toml; stdlib tomllib on 3.11+, tiny flat parser before."""
    if tomllib is not None:
        try:
            return tomllib.loads(text)
        except Exception as exc:  # tomllib.TOMLDecodeError, ValueError
            raise UsageError(f"config.toml is not valid TOML: {exc}") from exc
    return _parse_flat_toml(text)


def config_path() -> Path:
    override = os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_CONFIG")
    if override:
        return Path(override).expanduser()
    return DEFAULT_CONFIG_PATH


def load_config_data(path: Optional[Path] = None) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Read config.toml. A missing file is an empty config."""
    cfg_path = path.expanduser() if path is not None else config_path()
    try:
        text = cfg_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {}
    except OSError as exc:
        raise UsageError(f"cannot read config {cfg_path}: {exc}") from exc
    try:
        st = cfg_path.stat()
        if st.st_mode & 0o077:
            eprint(f"warn {cfg_path} mode {st.st_mode & 0o777:o} should be 0600")
    except OSError:
        pass
    data = parse_toml(text)
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}


def _clean_ident(value: str, what: str, max_chars: int) -> str:
    text = value.strip()
    if not text or "\n" in text or "\r" in text:
        raise UsageError(f"{what} is empty or contains a newline")
    if len(text) > max_chars:
        raise UsageError(f"{what} longer than {max_chars} characters")
    return text


def config_value(data: dict[str, Any], env_name: str, key: str) -> Any:
    """Env wins over the file (env may legitimately be an empty string)."""
    if env_name in os.environ:
        return os.environ[env_name]
    return data.get(key)


def identity_from_data(data: dict[str, Any]) -> tuple[str, str]:
    who_raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_WHO", "who")
    source_raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_SOURCE", "source")
    who = (
        _clean_ident(str(who_raw), "WHO", MAX_WHO_CHARS)
        if str(who_raw or "").strip()
        else DEFAULT_WHO
    )
    source = (
        _clean_ident(str(source_raw), "SOURCE", MAX_SOURCE_CHARS)
        if str(source_raw or "").strip()
        else DEFAULT_SOURCE
    )
    return who, source


def bot_name_from_data(data: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_BOT_NAME", "bot_name")
    if not str(raw or "").strip():
        return DEFAULT_BOT_NAME
    return _clean_ident(str(raw), "bot_name", MAX_BOT_NAME_CHARS)


def webhook_url_from_data(data: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_URL", "webhook_url")
    url = str(raw or "").strip()
    if not url:
        raise UsageError(
            "no webhook_url; run `asksoul init` or set ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_URL"
        )
    if not (url.startswith("https://") or url.startswith("http://")):
        raise UsageError("webhook_url must start with http:// or https://")
    return url


def resolve_secret(data: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    """ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET > secret_cmd > secret_file (mode 0600)."""
    env_secret = os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET")
    if env_secret is not None and env_secret.strip():
        return env_secret.strip()

    cmd_raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_SECRET_CMD", "secret_cmd")
    cmd = str(cmd_raw or "").strip()
    if cmd:
        try:
            proc = subprocess.run(
                cmd,
                shell=True,
                capture_output=True,
                text=True,
                timeout=15,
                check=False,
            )
        except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as exc:
            raise UsageError(f"secret_cmd failed: {exc}") from exc
        secret = proc.stdout.strip()
        if proc.returncode != 0:
            raise UsageError(f"secret_cmd exited {proc.returncode}")
        if not secret:
            raise UsageError("secret_cmd printed an empty secret")
        return secret

    file_raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_SECRET_FILE", "secret_file")
    file_text = str(file_raw or "").strip()
    if file_text:
        path = Path(file_text).expanduser()
        try:
            st = path.stat()
        except OSError as exc:
            raise UsageError(f"cannot read secret_file {path}: {exc}") from exc
        if st.st_mode & 0o077:
            raise UsageError(
                f"secret_file {path} mode {st.st_mode & 0o777:o} must be 0600"
            )
        try:
            secret = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip()
        except OSError as exc:
            raise UsageError(f"cannot read secret_file {path}: {exc}") from exc
        if not secret:
            raise UsageError(f"secret_file {path} is empty")
        return secret

    raise UsageError(
        "no webhook secret; set ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET, or configure "
        "secret_cmd / secret_file (see `asksoul init`)"
    )


def load_runtime_config(require_webhook: bool = True) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Resolve config + env. With require_webhook=False (test hook), the URL
    and secret may be absent; identity and bot name are still resolved."""
    data = load_config_data()
    who, source = identity_from_data(data)
    bot_name = bot_name_from_data(data)
    url = secret = ""
    if require_webhook:
        url = webhook_url_from_data(data)
        secret = resolve_secret(data)
    return {
        "url": url,
        "secret": secret,
        "who": who,
        "source": source,
        "bot_name": bot_name,
        "data": data,
    }


def peek_config() -> tuple[str, str, str]:
    """WHO/SOURCE/bot_name for --help. Config and env are optional."""
    try:
        data = load_config_data()
        who, source = identity_from_data(data)
        bot_name = bot_name_from_data(data)
        return who, source, bot_name
    except (UsageError, OSError):
        return DEFAULT_WHO, DEFAULT_SOURCE, DEFAULT_BOT_NAME


def render_help(who: str, source: str, bot_name: str = DEFAULT_BOT_NAME) -> str:
    return (
        HELP.replace("{bot}", bot_name)
        .replace("{who}", who)
        .replace("{source}", source)
        .replace("{version}", VERSION)
    )


def which_tailscale() -> str:
    override = os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_TAILSCALE")
    if override:
        if os.access(override, os.X_OK):
            return override
        raise SetupError("ASKSOUL_TAILSCALE is not executable")
    for cand in TAILSCALE_CANDIDATES:
        if os.path.sep in cand:
            if os.access(cand, os.X_OK):
                return cand
        else:
            found = shutil.which(cand)
            if found:
                return found
    raise SetupError("tailscale not found")


def run_tailscale(args: list[str], timeout: float = 8.0) -> str:
    bin_path = which_tailscale()
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(
            [bin_path, *args],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            timeout=timeout,
            check=False,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as exc:
        raise SetupError(f"tailscale {' '.join(args)} failed") from exc
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        raise SetupError(f"tailscale {' '.join(args)} exit {proc.returncode}")
    return proc.stdout


def first_ipv4_line(text: str) -> str:
    for line in text.splitlines():
        ip = line.strip()
        if ip and ":" not in ip:
            return ip
    raise SetupError("no Tailscale IPv4 in command output")


def self_bind_ipv4(data: dict[str, Any]) -> str:
    """Local address to listen on: config bind > ASKSOUL_BIND > tailscale."""
    override = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_BIND", "bind")
    if str(override or "").strip():
        return str(override).strip()
    try:
        return first_ipv4_line(run_tailscale(["ip", "-4"]))
    except SetupError as exc:
        raise SetupError(
            "cannot determine the bind address; set `bind` in config.toml "
            "or ASKSOUL_BIND, or install Tailscale"
        ) from exc


def _accept_entries(data: dict[str, Any]) -> list[str]:
    raw = config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_ACCEPT", "accept")
    entries: list[str] = []
    if raw is None:
        return entries
    values = raw if isinstance(raw, list) else str(raw).split(",")
    for value in values:
        if isinstance(value, str):
            entries.extend(part.strip() for part in value.split(",") if part.strip())
        elif value is not None:
            entries.append(str(value).strip())
    return entries


def resolve_accept_host(value: str) -> set[str]:
    """One accept entry -> IPv4 literal(s) or a CIDR string."""
    text = value.strip()
    if not text:
        return set()
    try:
        address = ipaddress.ip_address(text)
    except ValueError:
        address = None
    if address is not None:
        if address.version != 4:
            raise SetupError(f"accept {text!r} is not IPv4")
        return {text}
    try:
        network = ipaddress.ip_network(text, strict=False)
    except ValueError:
        network = None
    if network is not None:
        if network.version != 4:
            raise SetupError(f"accept {text!r} is not IPv4")
        return {str(network)}
    try:
        infos = socket.getaddrinfo(text, None, socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    except OSError as exc:
        raise SetupError(f"cannot resolve accept host {text!r}") from exc
    ips = {str(info[4][0]) for info in infos}
    if not ips:
        raise SetupError(f"accept host {text!r} resolved to no IPv4 address")
    return ips


def ssh_host_ipv4s(alias: str) -> set[str]:
    """Resolve an ssh config Host's HostName (accept_ssh_host)."""
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(
            ["ssh", "-G", alias],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            timeout=8,
            check=False,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as exc:
        raise SetupError(f"ssh -G {alias} failed") from exc
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        raise SetupError(f"ssh -G {alias} exit {proc.returncode}")
    for line in proc.stdout.splitlines():
        parts = line.split()
        if len(parts) >= 2 and parts[0].lower() == "hostname":
            return resolve_accept_host(parts[1].strip())
    raise SetupError(f"no HostName in ssh -G {alias}")


def accept_list(data: dict[str, Any]) -> set[str]:
    """Peers allowed to dial back: config/env accept + optional ssh Host."""
    entries = _accept_entries(data)
    ssh_host = str(
        config_value(data, "ASKSOUL_ACCEPT_SSH_HOST", "accept_ssh_host") or ""
    ).strip()
    allowed: set[str] = set()
    for entry in entries:
        allowed |= resolve_accept_host(entry)
    if ssh_host:
        allowed |= ssh_host_ipv4s(ssh_host)
    if not allowed:
        raise SetupError(
            "empty accept allowlist; set `accept` in config.toml or "
            "ASKSOUL_ACCEPT to the bot computer's IP or hostname"
        )
    return allowed


def peer_allowed(peer_ip: str, allow: set[str]) -> bool:
    """Exact IP match or membership in a configured CIDR."""
    try:
        addr = ipaddress.ip_address(peer_ip)
    except ValueError:
        return peer_ip in allow
    for entry in allow:
        if entry == peer_ip:
            return True
        try:
            network = ipaddress.ip_network(entry, strict=False)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if network.version == addr.version and addr in network:
            return True
    return False


def bind_listener(host: str) -> tuple[socket.socket, int]:
    sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    try:
        if hasattr(sock, "set_inheritable"):
            sock.set_inheritable(False)
        sock.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_REUSEADDR, 1)
        sock.bind((host, 0))
        sock.listen(8)
        port = int(sock.getsockname()[1])
    except OSError as exc:
        sock.close()
        raise SetupError(f"bind {host}:0 failed") from exc
    return sock, port


def b64encode(data: bytes) -> str:
    return base64.b64encode(data).decode("ascii")


def b64decode(text: str) -> Optional[bytes]:
    try:
        raw = text.encode("ascii")
    except (UnicodeEncodeError, AttributeError):
        return None
    try:
        return base64.b64decode(raw, validate=True)
    except (ValueError, TypeError):
        try:
            return base64.b64decode(raw)
        except (ValueError, TypeError):
            return None


def make_key() -> bytes:
    return secrets.token_bytes(32)


def build_payload(
    message: str,
    reply: dict[str, Any],
    session_id: str,
    source: str = DEFAULT_SOURCE,
    who: str = DEFAULT_WHO,
    sender_type: str = "user-cli",
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """The webhook body. session_id and reply are required and always written."""
    return {
        "source": source,
        "who": who,
        "sender_type": sender_type,
        "intent": "asksoul",
        "message": message,
        "reply": reply,
        "session_id": session_id,
    }


def reply_note(who: str = DEFAULT_WHO) -> str:
    """The reply.note string sent to the bot with every webhook."""
    del who  # kept for signature compatibility; the note speaks as "the CLI"
    return (
        "Dial host:port with this key. hmac-sha256-v1: "
        "mac=HMAC-SHA256(key, body_utf8). Line-delimited JSON both ways, one "
        "whole line + flush per frame. Every frame carries this session_id. "
        "One active connection at a time; sequential reconnects OK. Every "
        "frame needs kind, one of five (missing or other kinds are "
        "discarded): status = control/diagnostic (the CLI prints it to "
        "stderr only); msg = text (the CLI prints it to stdout; body ends "
        "with \\n); relayed = hand-off receipt: the receiver handed the "
        "message to the named bot (body = bot name); it does not mean that "
        "bot received or read it; close = ends the session; ack = the dialer "
        "named in from has received this session's latest line(s) (empty "
        "body; the dialer sends it automatically on every dial, before its "
        "other frames; it is not an answer). Frames may carry from = the "
        "sender's own name (1..64 chars, no [ ] or control chars); with "
        "from, mac=HMAC-SHA256(key, from_utf8 + \"\\n\" + body_utf8). A frame "
        "may also carry queued_at (ISO 8601 with seconds and offset, the "
        "original send attempt; msg or relayed only, and only with from); "
        "then mac=HMAC-SHA256(key, from_utf8 + \"\\0\" + queued_at + \"\\n\" "
        "+ body_utf8). The CLI shows it as queued at that time; the "
        "outbox sets it when it flushes a stored frame. The CLI prints a msg "
        "as \"[<from>] <body>\", a relayed as \"# relayed: <name> (by "
        "<from>)\" and an ack as \"# ack (by <from>)\", with ? when from is "
        "absent. Disconnecting without close does not end the session; the "
        "listener keeps waiting. The CLI waits until close or its timeout; "
        "timeout_sec is an idle timeout, reset by any frame from the "
        "receiver or any line the caller sends. A relayed makes that turn "
        "exit 6 and it will not resend, and a msg may still arrive on this "
        "session before close; an ack with no msg and no relayed makes the "
        "turn exit 9. The same session_id may arrive again in a new webhook "
        "carrying the same host, port and key: that is the caller's next "
        "line in this same session, dial in as usual. Webhooks with the same "
        "session_id belong to one thread. Every webhook carries a reply "
        "channel. The receiver decides what to do with the message: answer "
        "it, hand it to another bot, or ask back; a hand-off may be "
        "confirmed with relayed. Bot-side helper: `asksoul-talk` on PATH "
        "(--from NAME; the main bot name defaults to the configured "
        "bot_name), subcommands send, relayed, close, ask: one-shot send "
        "(kind msg), relayed --to NAME, close; ask --wait SEC --body TEXT "
        "sends, keeps the connection and prints the caller's next line "
        "(exit 0 got it, 3 timeout, 7 closed), for when an answer is "
        "expected. A line the caller sends while no bot is connected comes "
        "as that new webhook."
    )


def reply_object(
    host: str,
    port: int,
    timeout_sec: int,
    key: bytes,
    who: str = DEFAULT_WHO,
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    return {
        "required": True,
        "mode": "session",
        "transport": "tcp-tailnet",
        "host": host,
        "port": port,
        "timeout_sec": timeout_sec,
        "crypto": {
            "alg": ALG,
            "key_b64": b64encode(key),
        },
        "accept": "session",
        "note": reply_note(who),
    }


def _retryable_http(code: int) -> bool:
    """429 and 5xx are worth a retry; other HTTP codes are not."""
    return code == 429 or 500 <= code <= 599


def post_webhook(url: str, sender_key: str, payload: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    """POST the payload, retrying network errors, timeouts, 429 and 5xx.

    Up to WEBHOOK_ATTEMPTS tries, sleeping WEBHOOK_BACKOFF_SEC between
    them. A WebhookError detail names the attempts made and the last
    error.
    """
    body = json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")).encode("utf-8")
    auth = sender_key if sender_key.lower().startswith("bearer ") else f"Bearer {sender_key}"
    req = urllib.request.Request(
        url,
        data=body,
        method="POST",
        headers={
            "Content-Type": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "Authorization": auth,
            "User-Agent": USER_AGENT,
            "Accept": "application/json",
        },
    )
    attempts = 0
    last = ""
    while True:
        attempts += 1
        retry = False
        try:
            with _OPENER.open(req, timeout=WEBHOOK_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SEC) as resp:
                code = getattr(resp, "status", None) or resp.getcode()
                try:
                    resp.read(4096)
                except OSError:
                    pass
            if code and 200 <= int(code) < 300:
                return
            last = f"HTTP {code or '?'}"
            retry = _retryable_http(int(code or 0))
        except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:
            code = int(getattr(exc, "code", 0) or 0)
            try:
                exc.read(256)
            except OSError:
                pass
            last = f"HTTP {code or '?'}"
            retry = _retryable_http(code)
        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, OSError):
            last = "network error"
            retry = True
        if not retry or attempts >= WEBHOOK_ATTEMPTS:
            word = "attempt" if attempts == 1 else "attempts"
            raise WebhookError(f"{attempts} {word}, last: {last}", attempts)
        pause = WEBHOOK_BACKOFF_SEC[attempts - 1]
        eprint(
            f"webhook attempt {attempts}/{WEBHOOK_ATTEMPTS} failed "
            f"({last}), retrying in {pause} s"
        )
        time.sleep(pause)


def pop_json_lines(buf: bytearray) -> list[bytes]:
    lines: list[bytes] = []
    while True:
        nl = buf.find(b"\n")
        if nl == -1:
            break
        line = bytes(buf[:nl])
        del buf[: nl + 1]
        if line.endswith(b"\r"):
            line = line[:-1]
        lines.append(line)
    if len(buf) > MAX_FRAME_BYTES:
        eprint("frame exceeds 1MiB, discarded")
        buf.clear()
    return lines


def valid_from_name(name: object) -> bool:
    """Frame "from": 1..64 chars, no control chars, no [ or ], not only spaces."""
    if not isinstance(name, str) or not 1 <= len(name) <= MAX_FROM_CHARS:
        return False
    if not name.strip():
        return False
    if any(ord(ch) < 32 or ord(ch) == 127 for ch in name):
        return False
    return "[" not in name and "]" not in name


def valid_queued_at(value: object) -> bool:
    """Frame "queued_at": ISO 8601, seconds, explicit offset."""
    return isinstance(value, str) and QUEUED_AT_RE.fullmatch(value) is not None


def frame_mac(
    key: bytes,
    from_name: Optional[str],
    body: bytes,
    queued_at: Optional[str] = None,
) -> bytes:
    """Canonical MAC input (bytes, UTF-8), by what the frame carries:
      no queued_at, no from:  body
      no queued_at, from:     from + "\\n" + body
      queued_at, from:        from + "\\0" + queued_at + "\\n" + body

    queued_at is valid only together with from; calling this with
    queued_at and no from is a bug in the caller.
    """
    if queued_at is None:
        if from_name is None:
            return hmac.new(key, body, hashlib.sha256).digest()
        data = from_name.encode("utf-8") + b"\n" + body
    else:
        if from_name is None:
            raise ValueError("queued_at requires from")
        data = (
            from_name.encode("utf-8")
            + b"\x00"
            + queued_at.encode("utf-8")
            + b"\n"
            + body
        )
    return hmac.new(key, data, hashlib.sha256).digest()


def verify_frame(
    line: bytes,
    key: bytes,
    expect_session_id: Optional[str] = None,
) -> tuple[
    bool, str, Optional[str], Optional[bytes], Optional[str], Optional[str]
]:
    """(ok, reason, kind, body, from_name, queued_at).

    reason never contains the key. queued_at is returned only for a
    validated value on msg/relayed; status/close/ack reject it.
    """
    if not line.strip():
        return False, "empty frame, discarded", None, None, None, None
    try:
        obj = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):
        return False, "frame is not JSON, discarded", None, None, None, None
    if not isinstance(obj, dict):
        return False, "frame is not a JSON object, discarded", None, None, None, None
    if obj.get("v") != 1:
        return False, "bad frame v, discarded", None, None, None, None
    if obj.get("alg") != ALG:
        return False, "bad frame alg, discarded", None, None, None, None
    kind = obj.get("kind")
    if not isinstance(kind, str) or kind not in INBOUND_KINDS:
        return False, "bad frame kind, discarded", None, None, None, None
    mac_b64 = obj.get("mac_b64")
    body_b64 = obj.get("body_b64")
    if not isinstance(mac_b64, str) or not isinstance(body_b64, str):
        return False, "frame missing mac_b64/body_b64, discarded", None, None, None, None
    mac = b64decode(mac_b64)
    body = b64decode(body_b64)
    if mac is None or body is None:
        return False, "frame base64 invalid, discarded", None, None, None, None
    from_name: Optional[str] = None
    if "from" in obj:
        raw_from = obj["from"]
        if not valid_from_name(raw_from):
            return False, "bad frame from, discarded", None, None, None, None
        from_name = raw_from
    queued_at: Optional[str] = None
    if "queued_at" in obj:
        raw_queued = obj["queued_at"]
        if not valid_queued_at(raw_queued):
            return False, "bad frame queued_at, discarded", None, None, None, None
        if kind not in (KIND_MSG, KIND_RELAYED):
            return False, "bad frame queued_at, discarded", None, None, None, None
        if from_name is None:
            return False, "bad frame queued_at, discarded", None, None, None, None
        queued_at = raw_queued
    expected = frame_mac(key, from_name, body, queued_at)
    if len(mac) != len(expected) or not hmac.compare_digest(mac, expected):
        return False, "bad MAC, discarded", None, None, None, None
    frame_sid = obj.get("session_id")
    if not isinstance(frame_sid, str) or not frame_sid:
        return False, "bad frame session_id, discarded", None, None, None, None
    if expect_session_id and frame_sid != expect_session_id:
        return False, "session_id mismatch, discarded", None, None, None, None
    if kind == KIND_STATUS:
        extra = obj.get("status")
        if extra is not None:
            try:
                token = body.decode("utf-8")
            except UnicodeDecodeError:
                return False, "bad status, discarded", None, None, None, None
            if extra != token:
                return False, "status field mismatch, discarded", None, None, None, None
        return True, "", KIND_STATUS, body, from_name, None
    return True, "", kind, body, from_name, queued_at


def build_frame(
    kind: str,
    body: bytes,
    key: bytes,
    session_id: str,
) -> bytes:
    """One frame line. session_id is required and always written.

    The CLI's own outbound frames carry no "from" and no queued_at: the MAC
    is over body.
    """
    mac = frame_mac(key, None, body)
    obj: dict[str, Any] = {
        "v": 1,
        "alg": ALG,
        "kind": kind,
        "session_id": session_id,
        "mac_b64": b64encode(mac),
        "body_b64": b64encode(body),
    }
    return json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")).encode("utf-8") + b"\n"


def close_quietly(sock: Optional[socket.socket]) -> None:
    if sock is None:
        return
    try:
        sock.shutdown(socket.SHUT_RDWR)
    except OSError:
        pass
    try:
        sock.close()
    except OSError:
        pass


def prepare_conn(conn: socket.socket) -> None:
    if hasattr(conn, "set_inheritable"):
        conn.set_inheritable(False)
    try:
        conn.setsockopt(socket.SOL_SOCKET, socket.SO_KEEPALIVE, 1)
    except OSError:
        pass
    try:
        conn.setsockopt(socket.IPPROTO_TCP, socket.TCP_NODELAY, 1)
    except OSError:
        pass
    conn.settimeout(None)


def send_raw(conn: socket.socket, data: bytes, deadline: float) -> bool:
    remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
    if remaining <= 0:
        return False
    try:
        conn.settimeout(remaining)
        conn.sendall(data)
        return True
    except OSError:
        return False
    finally:
        try:
            conn.settimeout(None)
        except OSError:
            pass


def conn_is_idle(conn: socket.socket, buf: bytearray) -> bool:
    if buf:
        return False
    try:
        ready, _, _ = select.select([conn], [], [], 0)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return True
    if not ready:
        return True
    try:
        peeked = conn.recv(1, socket.MSG_PEEK)
    except OSError:
        return True
    return not peeked


def emit_status(body: bytes) -> None:
    try:
        text = body.decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError:
        text = body.decode("utf-8", "replace")
    sys.stderr.write(f"# status: {text}\n")
    try:
        sys.stderr.flush()
    except OSError:
        pass


def emit_frame_meta(kind: str, body: bytes, sent: bool = False) -> None:
    extra = " sent" if sent else ""
    sys.stderr.write(f"# frame: kind={kind} len={len(body)}{extra}\n")
    try:
        sys.stderr.flush()
    except OSError:
        pass


def emit_stdout(body: bytes) -> None:
    sys.stdout.buffer.write(body)
    sys.stdout.buffer.flush()


class _DaemonStop(Exception):
    """Raised in the background session by its SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP hooks."""


def _daemon_signal(signum: int, frame: Any) -> None:
    raise _DaemonStop


class LogWriter:
    """Daemon sys.stderr: every diagnostic line gets a local timestamp."""

    def __init__(self, stream: Any) -> None:
        self._stream = stream
        self._carry = ""

    def write(self, text: str) -> int:
        self._carry += text
        while "\n" in self._carry:
            line, self._carry = self._carry.split("\n", 1)
            self._stream.write(f"{time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')} {line}\n")
        try:
            self._stream.flush()
        except OSError:
            pass
        return len(text)

    def flush(self) -> None:
        if self._carry:
            self.write("\n")
        try:
            self._stream.flush()
        except OSError:
            pass


def decode_body(body: bytes) -> str:
    try:
        return body.decode("utf-8")
    except UnicodeDecodeError:
        return body.decode("utf-8", "replace")


def message_text(body: bytes) -> str:
    """A msg body as the webhook "message": decoded, one trailing \\n off."""
    text = decode_body(body)
    return text[:-1] if text.endswith("\n") else text


def queued_display(queued_at: str) -> str:
    """A validated queued_at as "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM <offset>" (Z as +00:00)."""
    offset = "+00:00" if queued_at.endswith("Z") else queued_at[19:]
    return f"{queued_at[:10]} {queued_at[11:16]} {offset}"


def format_msg(
    from_name: Optional[str], body: str, queued_at: Optional[str] = None
) -> str:
    """A turn's msg line: the speaker prefix, body as-is (first line only)."""
    if queued_at:
        return (
            f"[{from_name or '?'}, queued {queued_display(queued_at)}] {body}"
        )
    return f"[{from_name or '?'}] {body}"



def classify_delivery(got_relayed: bool, got_ack: bool, got_text: bool) -> str:
    """Map turn flags to the fixed DELIVERY status word."""
    if got_relayed:
        return "relayed"
    if got_ack or got_text:
        return "ack"
    return "unconfirmed"


def emit_delivery(status: str, as_json: bool) -> None:
    """Always print 'DELIVERY <status>'; with --json also print JSON."""
    line = f"DELIVERY {status}\n"
    try:
        emit_stdout(line.encode("utf-8"))
    except BrokenPipeError:
        pass
    if as_json:
        payload = json.dumps({"delivery": status}, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
        try:
            emit_stdout(payload.encode("utf-8"))
        except BrokenPipeError:
            pass


def format_ack(from_name: Optional[str]) -> str:
    """A turn's ack line: the dialer named in from received the last line(s)."""
    return f"# ack (by {from_name or '?'})\n"


def format_relayed(
    from_name: Optional[str], name: str, queued_at: Optional[str] = None
) -> str:
    """A turn's relayed line: the hand-off to <name>, sent by <from or ?>."""
    if queued_at:
        return (
            f"# relayed: {name} (by {from_name or '?'}, "
            f"queued {queued_display(queued_at)})\n"
        )
    return f"# relayed: {name} (by {from_name or '?'})\n"


def state_home() -> Path:
    return Path(
        os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or (Path.home() / ".local" / "state")
    ).expanduser()


def sessions_root() -> Path:
    return state_home() / "asksoul" / "sessions"


def session_dir_for(session_id: str) -> Path:
    """One dir per session: hash(session_id)[:16], an internal path key only.

    The session id is in meta.json. The hash keeps the unix socket path
    short and safe.
    """
    digest = hashlib.sha256(session_id.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()[:16]
    return sessions_root() / digest


def makedirs_private(path: Path) -> None:
    """mkdir -p, mode 0700 for every directory this call creates."""
    missing: list[Path] = []
    cur = path
    while not cur.exists() and cur.parent != cur:
        missing.append(cur)
        cur = cur.parent
    for directory in reversed(missing):
        try:
            directory.mkdir(mode=SESSION_DIR_MODE)
        except FileExistsError:
            pass


def pid_alive(pid: int) -> bool:
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        return True
    except OSError:
        return False
    return True


def read_session_meta(session_dir: Path) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:
    try:
        raw = (session_dir / META_NAME).read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    except OSError:
        return None
    try:
        meta = json.loads(raw)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return None
    return meta if isinstance(meta, dict) else None


def live_session(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:
    """The session's meta when it is live (pid alive and id matches)."""
    meta = read_session_meta(session_dir)
    if meta is None or meta.get("id") != session_id:
        return None
    pid = meta.get("pid")
    if not isinstance(pid, int) or not pid_alive(pid):
        return None
    return meta


def session_state(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> str:
    """What -s ID finds: live, ended (lingering unread frames) or stale."""
    meta = live_session(session_dir, session_id)
    if meta is None:
        return STATE_STALE
    if isinstance(meta.get("ended"), str):
        return STATE_ENDED
    return STATE_LIVE


def live_daemon_pid(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> Optional[int]:
    """meta.json's pid while it is this session's and still alive."""
    meta = read_session_meta(session_dir)
    if meta is None or meta.get("id") != session_id:
        return None
    pid = meta.get("pid")
    if not isinstance(pid, int) or not pid_alive(pid):
        return None
    return pid


def write_session_meta(session_dir: Path, meta: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    path = session_dir / META_NAME
    path.write_text(json.dumps(meta, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    try:
        os.chmod(path, SESSION_FILE_MODE)
    except OSError:
        pass


def caller_command(ppid: int) -> str:
    """`ps -o command= -p PPID`, truncated to 200 chars, best effort."""
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run(
            ["ps", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(ppid)],
            capture_output=True,
            text=True,
            timeout=5,
            check=False,
        )
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return ""
    return proc.stdout.strip()[:CALLER_CMD_CHARS]


def build_session_meta(
    session_id: str,
    who: str,
    source: str,
    host: str,
    port: int,
    timeout_sec: int,
    message: str,
) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """meta.json for a new session. The daemon fills in its own pid."""
    ppid = os.getppid()
    try:
        cwd = os.getcwd()
    except OSError:
        cwd = ""
    return {
        "id": session_id,
        "pid": 0,
        "created": time.time(),
        "who": who,
        "source": source,
        "host": host,
        "port": port,
        "timeout_sec": timeout_sec,
        "message_head": message[:MESSAGE_HEAD_CHARS],
        "caller": {"ppid": ppid, "cwd": cwd, "cmd": caller_command(ppid)},
    }


def format_age(seconds: float) -> str:
    total = int(max(0.0, seconds))
    days, rest = divmod(total, 86400)
    hours, rest = divmod(rest, 3600)
    mins, secs = divmod(rest, 60)
    if days:
        return f"{days}d{hours}h"
    if hours:
        return f"{hours}h{mins}m"
    if mins:
        return f"{mins}m{secs}s"
    return f"{secs}s"


def connect_ctl(session_dir: Path, wait: float = 0.0) -> Optional[socket.socket]:
    """Connect to the session's control socket, retrying for wait seconds."""
    path = session_dir / CTL_NAME
    deadline = time.monotonic() + max(0.0, wait)
    while True:
        conn = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
        try:
            conn.connect(str(path))
        except OSError:
            close_quietly(conn)
            if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                return None
            time.sleep(CTL_RETRY_SEC)
            continue
        prepare_conn(conn)
        return conn


def connect_session(
    session_dir: Path, session_id: str, wait: float
) -> Optional[socket.socket]:
    """Wait for a live session and its control socket (the session process)."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + max(0.0, wait)
    while True:
        if live_session(session_dir, session_id) is not None:
            conn = connect_ctl(session_dir)
            if conn is not None:
                return conn
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return None
        time.sleep(CTL_RETRY_SEC)


def send_event(conn: socket.socket, obj: dict[str, Any]) -> bool:
    """One JSON line on the control socket."""
    data = (
        json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(",", ":")).encode("utf-8")
        + b"\n"
    )
    return send_raw(conn, data, time.monotonic() + EVENT_SEND_TIMEOUT)


def read_json_line(conn: socket.socket, timeout: float) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:
    """Read one JSON object line from the control socket, or None."""
    buf = bytearray()
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
    while True:
        remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
        if remaining <= 0:
            return None
        try:
            ready, _, _ = select.select([conn], [], [], remaining)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return None
        if not ready:
            return None
        try:
            chunk = conn.recv(4096)
        except OSError:
            return None
        if not chunk:
            return None
        buf.extend(chunk)
        lines = pop_json_lines(buf)
        if not lines:
            continue
        try:
            obj = json.loads(lines[0].decode("utf-8"))
        except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            return None
        return obj if isinstance(obj, dict) else None


def bind_ctl(session_dir: Path) -> socket.socket:
    """The AF_UNIX stream socket the daemon serves clients on (mode 0600)."""
    path = session_dir / CTL_NAME
    try:
        os.unlink(path)
    except OSError:
        pass
    sock = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX, socket.SOCK_STREAM)
    try:
        if hasattr(sock, "set_inheritable"):
            sock.set_inheritable(False)
        sock.bind(str(path))
        os.chmod(path, SESSION_FILE_MODE)
        sock.listen(8)
    except OSError:
        sock.close()
        raise
    return sock


_DAEMON_PROCS: list[subprocess.Popen] = []


def spawn_daemon(
    session_dir: Path,
    meta: dict[str, Any],
    listener: socket.socket,
    key: bytes,
    allow: set[str],
    timeout_sec: int,
    session_id: str,
    who: str,
    source: str,
    reply_meta: dict[str, Any],
    url: str,
    sender_key: str,
) -> None:
    """Exec the background session on a fresh interpreter; this process returns.

    Never fork: the parent has already run getaddrinfo for the webhook POST,
    and a forked copy inherits that initialized network state — on macOS the
    daemon's next getaddrinfo (its -s rewake POST) then crashes inside
    Network.framework. The exec'd child gets the session state as one JSON
    line on stdin (secrets travel only on this pipe, never argv/env/disk)
    and the bound listener as an inherited fd.
    """
    data = (
        json.dumps(
            {
                "session_dir": str(session_dir),
                "meta": meta,
                "key": b64encode(key),
                "allow": sorted(allow),
                "timeout_sec": timeout_sec,
                "session_id": session_id,
                "who": who,
                "source": source,
                "reply_meta": reply_meta,
                "url": url,
                "sender_key": sender_key,
            },
            ensure_ascii=False,
            separators=(",", ":"),
        ).encode("utf-8")
        + b"\n"
    )
    env = os.environ.copy()
    env[DAEMON_FD_ENV] = str(listener.fileno())
    proc = subprocess.Popen(
        [sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__)],
        stdin=subprocess.PIPE,
        stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL,
        stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,
        close_fds=True,
        pass_fds=(listener.fileno(),),
        start_new_session=True,
        env=env,
    )
    if proc.stdin is not None:
        try:
            proc.stdin.write(data)
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            proc.stdin.close()
        except OSError:
            pass
    # Keep the Popen object and never wait: the child is the long-lived
    # daemon, not a job of ours (the parent exits after the first turn).
    _DAEMON_PROCS.append(proc)


def log_daemon_crash(session_dir: Optional[Path], text: str) -> None:
    """Best effort: an early daemon traceback lands in the session log."""
    if session_dir is None or not session_dir.is_dir():
        return
    stamp = time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
    try:
        with open(session_dir / LOG_NAME, "a", encoding="utf-8") as out:
            out.write(f"{stamp} daemon init failed\n")
            for line in text.rstrip("\n").splitlines():
                out.write(f"{stamp} {line}\n")
        os.chmod(session_dir / LOG_NAME, SESSION_FILE_MODE)
    except OSError:
        pass


def daemon_entry() -> int:
    """ASKSOUL_DAEMON_FD: this process is the exec'd background session.

    Internal only (spawn_daemon sets the marker): one JSON object on stdin
    carries the session state, the inherited fd is the bound listener.
    """
    fd_raw = os.environ.pop(DAEMON_FD_ENV, "")
    session_dir: Optional[Path] = None
    try:
        data = json.loads(sys.stdin.buffer.read().decode("utf-8"))
        if not isinstance(data, dict):
            raise ValueError("daemon init is not a JSON object")
        session_dir = Path(str(data["session_dir"]))
        key = b64decode(str(data["key"]))
        if key is None:
            raise ValueError("daemon init key is not base64")
        # family/type come from the inherited fd itself.
        listener = socket.socket(fileno=int(fd_raw))
        run_daemon(
            session_dir,
            data["meta"],
            listener,
            key,
            set(data["allow"]),
            int(data["timeout_sec"]),
            str(data["session_id"]),
            str(data["who"]),
            str(data["source"]),
            data["reply_meta"],
            str(data["url"]),
            str(data["sender_key"]),
        )
    except BaseException:
        # run_daemon logs its own crashes; this is the init path before it.
        log_daemon_crash(session_dir, traceback.format_exc())
        return EXIT_SETUP
    return EXIT_OK


def run_daemon(
    session_dir: Path,
    meta: dict[str, Any],
    listener: socket.socket,
    key: bytes,
    allow: set[str],
    timeout_sec: int,
    session_id: str,
    who: str,
    source: str,
    reply_meta: dict[str, Any],
    url: str,
    sender_key: str,
) -> None:
    """The background session: the bot TCP side plus the control socket."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout_sec
    current: Optional[socket.socket] = None
    bot_buf = bytearray()
    events: deque[dict[str, Any]] = deque()
    client: Optional[socket.socket] = None
    client_buf = bytearray()
    conn: Optional[socket.socket] = None
    conn_buf = bytearray()
    bad_mac_streak = 0
    finished = False
    ctl: Optional[socket.socket] = None
    log_out: Optional[Any] = None

    def send_deadline() -> float:
        return time.monotonic() + EVENT_SEND_TIMEOUT

    def drop_current() -> None:
        nonlocal current
        close_quietly(current)
        current = None
        bot_buf.clear()

    def emit_event(obj: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
        """Deliver to the attached client, else keep it for the next one."""
        nonlocal client
        if client is not None:
            if send_event(client, obj):
                return
            eprint("ctl client write failed, dropped")
            close_quietly(client)
            client = None
        events.append(obj)

    def flush_events() -> None:
        nonlocal client
        while client is not None and events:
            if not send_event(client, events[0]):
                eprint("ctl client write failed, dropped")
                close_quietly(client)
                client = None
                return
            events.popleft()

    def add_client() -> None:
        """The pending connection takes the seat; any older one is replaced."""
        nonlocal client, conn
        if conn is None:
            return
        if client is not None:
            send_event(client, {"ev": "end", "reason": END_REPLACED})
            eprint("ctl client replaced")
            close_quietly(client)
            client_buf.clear()
        client = conn
        conn = None
        client_buf.extend(conn_buf)
        conn_buf.clear()
        flush_events()

    def wake_bot(message: str) -> Optional[WebhookError]:
        """Re-POST the webhook: same session, the user's next line.

        Returns None on success, else the WebhookError (its detail names
        the attempts made and the last error).
        """
        if os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_NO_WEBHOOK") == "1":
            out: dict[str, Any] = {
                "no_webhook_rewake": True,
                "message": message,
                "session_id": session_id,
                "port": meta["port"],
            }
            sys.stderr.write(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
            sys.stderr.flush()
            return None
        payload = build_payload(message, reply_meta, session_id, source, who)
        try:
            post_webhook(url, sender_key, payload)
        except WebhookError as exc:
            eprint(f"rewake webhook failed ({exc.detail})")
            return exc
        return None

    def user_msg(text: str) -> None:
        nonlocal deadline
        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout_sec
        body = text.encode("utf-8")
        if current is not None:
            data = build_frame(KIND_MSG, body, key, session_id)
            if send_raw(current, data, send_deadline()):
                emit_frame_meta(KIND_MSG, body, sent=True)
                emit_event({"ev": "sent"})
                return
            eprint("send failed, waiting for reconnect")
            drop_current()
        failure = wake_bot(message_text(body))
        if failure is None:
            emit_event({"ev": "rewoke"})
            return
        emit_event(
            {
                "ev": "webhook_failed",
                "attempts": failure.attempts,
                "detail": failure.detail,
            }
        )

    def info_event() -> dict[str, Any]:
        left = deadline - time.monotonic()
        return {
            "ev": "info",
            "id": session_id,
            "pid": os.getpid(),
            "idle_left": max(0, int(round(left))),
            "timeout_sec": timeout_sec,
            "who": who,
            "host": meta["host"],
            "port": meta["port"],
            "attached": client is not None,
            "bot": current is not None,
        }

    def serve_ctl_line(line: bytes, source: socket.socket) -> Optional[str]:
        """One control line from a client; the end reason if the session ends."""
        nonlocal conn, client, client_buf
        if not line.strip():
            return None
        try:
            obj = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
        except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):
            eprint("ctl line is not JSON, dropped")
            return None
        if not isinstance(obj, dict):
            eprint("ctl line is not a JSON object, dropped")
            return None
        op = obj.get("op")
        if op == OP_INFO:
            if not send_event(source, info_event()):
                eprint("ctl info reply failed")
                if source is client:
                    close_quietly(client)
                    client = None
                    client_buf.clear()
            if source is conn:
                close_quietly(conn)
                conn = None
                conn_buf.clear()
            return None
        if source is conn:
            add_client()
        if op == OP_ATTACH:
            return None
        if op == OP_MSG:
            body = obj.get("body")
            if not isinstance(body, str):
                eprint("ctl msg has no body, ignored")
                return None
            user_msg(body)
            return None
        if op == OP_CLOSE:
            if current is not None:
                data = build_frame(KIND_CLOSE, b"", key, session_id)
                if send_raw(current, data, send_deadline()):
                    emit_frame_meta(KIND_CLOSE, b"", sent=True)
                drop_current()
            return END_LOCAL_CLOSE
        eprint(f"ctl op {op!r} ignored")
        return None

    def serve_inbound(line: bytes) -> Optional[str]:
        """One frame from the bot. Returns an end reason when it ends us."""
        nonlocal bad_mac_streak, deadline
        ok, reason, kind, body, from_name, queued_at = verify_frame(
            line, key, session_id
        )
        if not ok or kind is None or body is None:
            eprint(reason)
            if reason.startswith("bad MAC"):
                bad_mac_streak += 1
                if bad_mac_streak == 1:
                    eprint(
                        "HMAC failed on this run's key (likely stale session "
                        "crypto). Start a new session."
                    )
                if bad_mac_streak >= BAD_MAC_ABORT_AFTER:
                    eprint(
                        f"aborting after {BAD_MAC_ABORT_AFTER} consecutive "
                        "bad MACs"
                    )
                    return END_BAD_MAC
            return None
        bad_mac_streak = 0
        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout_sec
        emit_frame_meta(kind, body)
        if kind == KIND_STATUS:
            emit_status(body)
            emit_event({"ev": "status", "body": decode_body(body)})
            return None
        if kind == KIND_MSG:
            emit_event(
                {
                    "ev": "msg",
                    "body": decode_body(body),
                    "from": from_name or None,
                    "queued_at": queued_at or None,
                }
            )
            return None
        if kind == KIND_RELAYED:
            emit_event(
                {
                    "ev": "relayed",
                    "name": decode_body(body).strip(),
                    "from": from_name or None,
                    "queued_at": queued_at or None,
                }
            )
            return None
        if kind == KIND_ACK:
            emit_event({"ev": "ack", "from": from_name or None})
            return None
        if kind == KIND_CLOSE:
            text = decode_body(body)
            if text:
                eprint(f"close {text}")
            emit_event({"ev": "close", "reason": text})
            return END_CLOSED
        return None

    def wait_first_client() -> None:
        """Let the opening caller attach before any bot frame is read.

        The default action prints the webhook JSON before the daemon
        starts, so a bot may be dialing in and talking before that
        foreground is back as a client. Holding the bot side back for a
        moment is what lets the first turn see a close or a bad-MAC abort
        instead of finding the session gone.
        """
        nonlocal conn
        grace = time.monotonic() + DAEMON_ATTACH_GRACE
        while client is None and conn is None and ctl is not None:
            wait = min(grace, deadline) - time.monotonic()
            if wait <= 0:
                return
            try:
                ready, _, _ = select.select([ctl, listener], [], [], wait)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                return
            if not ready:
                return
            if ctl in ready:
                try:
                    new_conn, _ = ctl.accept()
                except OSError:
                    return
                if new_conn is not None:
                    prepare_conn(new_conn)
                    conn = new_conn
                return
            # only the bot is ready: keep it queued until the client sits

    def daemon_loop() -> str:
        """Serve the bot and the client until the session ends."""
        nonlocal current, conn, client
        wait_first_client()
        while True:
            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                eprint("idle timeout, no close")
                return END_TIMEOUT
            rlist: list[Any] = [listener]
            if ctl is not None:
                rlist.append(ctl)
            if current is not None:
                rlist.append(current)
            if client is not None:
                rlist.append(client)
            if conn is not None:
                rlist.append(conn)
            try:
                ready, _, _ = select.select(rlist, [], [], remaining)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                eprint("select failed")
                return END_LOCAL_CLOSE
            if not ready:
                eprint("idle timeout, no close")
                return END_TIMEOUT

            # One recv per socket per select round: promoting the pending
            # connection to client must not make us read the same socket
            # twice off one stale readiness.
            bot_conn, pending_conn, client_conn = current, conn, client

            if ctl is not None and ctl in ready:
                try:
                    new_conn, _ = ctl.accept()
                except OSError:
                    new_conn = None
                if new_conn is not None:
                    if conn is not None:
                        eprint("ctl connection replaced")
                        close_quietly(conn)
                        conn_buf.clear()
                    prepare_conn(new_conn)
                    conn = new_conn

            if pending_conn is not None and pending_conn in ready:
                try:
                    chunk = pending_conn.recv(4096)
                except OSError:
                    chunk = b""
                if not chunk:
                    if pending_conn is conn:
                        close_quietly(conn)
                        conn = None
                        conn_buf.clear()
                else:
                    conn_buf.extend(chunk)
                    for line in pop_json_lines(conn_buf):
                        end = serve_ctl_line(line, pending_conn)
                        if end is not None:
                            return end

            if client_conn is not None and client_conn in ready:
                try:
                    chunk = client_conn.recv(4096)
                except OSError:
                    chunk = b""
                if not chunk:
                    if client_conn is client:
                        eprint("ctl client disconnected")
                        close_quietly(client)
                        client = None
                        client_buf.clear()
                else:
                    client_buf.extend(chunk)
                    for line in pop_json_lines(client_buf):
                        end = serve_ctl_line(line, client_conn)
                        if end is not None:
                            return end

            if listener in ready:
                try:
                    bot, addr = listener.accept()
                except OSError:
                    bot = None
                    addr = None
                if bot is not None:
                    peer_ip = addr[0] if addr else ""
                    if not peer_allowed(peer_ip, allow):
                        eprint(f"rejected peer {peer_ip}")
                        close_quietly(bot)
                    elif current is not None and not conn_is_idle(current, bot_buf):
                        eprint(f"rejected concurrent peer {peer_ip}")
                        close_quietly(bot)
                    else:
                        if current is not None:
                            eprint(f"peer replaced {peer_ip}")
                            drop_current()
                        prepare_conn(bot)
                        current = bot

            if bot_conn is not None and bot_conn in ready and bot_conn is current:
                try:
                    chunk = bot_conn.recv(4096)
                except OSError:
                    chunk = b""
                if not chunk:
                    if bot_buf:
                        eprint("incomplete frame, discarded")
                    drop_current()
                else:
                    bot_buf.extend(chunk)
                    for line in pop_json_lines(bot_buf):
                        end = serve_inbound(line)
                        if end is not None:
                            return end

    def finish(reason: str) -> None:
        nonlocal finished, client, conn, current, ctl
        if finished:
            return
        finished = True
        if client is not None:
            send_event(client, {"ev": "end", "reason": reason})
        for sock in (client, conn, current, ctl, listener):
            close_quietly(sock)
        client = None
        conn = None
        current = None
        ctl = None
        if log_out is not None:
            try:
                log_out.close()
            except OSError:
                pass
        shutil.rmtree(session_dir, ignore_errors=True)

    def setup() -> socket.socket:
        nonlocal log_out
        makedirs_private(session_dir)
        log_path = session_dir / LOG_NAME
        log_out = open(log_path, "a", encoding="utf-8")
        try:
            os.chmod(log_path, SESSION_FILE_MODE)
        except OSError:
            pass
        sys.stderr = LogWriter(log_out)
        for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
            signal.signal(sig, _daemon_signal)
        meta["pid"] = os.getpid()
        write_session_meta(session_dir, meta)
        server = bind_ctl(session_dir)
        eprint(
            f"daemon pid {os.getpid()} session {session_id} listening "
            f"{meta['host']}:{meta['port']} idle timeout {timeout_sec}s"
        )
        return server

    def linger(reason: str) -> None:
        """The bot is gone but its last frames are unread: keep them up to -t.

        Only the control socket stays open. The next client gets the unread
        events and then the end event; info answers without taking the seat.
        """
        nonlocal current, client, conn
        drop_current()
        close_quietly(listener)
        meta["ended"] = reason
        write_session_meta(session_dir, meta)
        eprint(f"session ended ({reason}); keeping unread frames up to {timeout_sec}s")
        # A client may already have been accepted but not promoted when the
        # end frame arrived in the same select round. Give it the queued
        # events now instead of waiting for a second connection that the
        # caller will never make.
        if conn is not None:
            if client is not None:
                close_quietly(client)
                client_buf.clear()
            client = conn
            conn = None
            client_buf.extend(conn_buf)
            conn_buf.clear()
            flush_events()
        until = time.monotonic() + timeout_sec
        while client is None and ctl is not None:
            left = until - time.monotonic()
            if left <= 0:
                eprint("unread frames expired")
                return
            try:
                ready, _, _ = select.select([ctl], [], [], left)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                return
            if not ready:
                eprint("unread frames expired")
                return
            try:
                new_conn, _ = ctl.accept()
            except OSError:
                continue
            prepare_conn(new_conn)
            obj = read_json_line(new_conn, CTL_REPLY_TIMEOUT) or {}
            if obj.get("op") == OP_INFO:
                info = info_event()
                info["ended"] = reason
                send_event(new_conn, info)
                close_quietly(new_conn)
                continue
            if obj.get("op") == OP_MSG:
                eprint("ctl msg after session end, not sent")
            client = new_conn
            flush_events()

    reason = END_LOCAL_CLOSE
    try:
        ctl = setup()
        reason = daemon_loop()
        if (
            reason in (END_CLOSED, END_TIMEOUT, END_BAD_MAC)
            and client is None
            and any(e.get("ev") != "status" for e in events)
        ):
            linger(reason)
    except _DaemonStop:
        eprint("stopped by signal, ending session")
    except BaseException:
        traceback.print_exc()
    finally:
        finish(reason)


def query_idle_left(session_dir: Path, meta: dict[str, Any]) -> int:
    """Idle seconds left, asked of the live daemon; -t if it cannot answer."""
    conn = connect_ctl(session_dir)
    if conn is not None:
        try:
            if send_event(conn, {"op": OP_INFO}):
                obj = read_json_line(conn, CTL_REPLY_TIMEOUT)
                if obj is not None:
                    left = obj.get("idle_left")
                    if isinstance(left, (int, float)):
                        return max(0, int(left))
        finally:
            close_quietly(conn)
    timeout_sec = meta.get("timeout_sec")
    return int(timeout_sec) if isinstance(timeout_sec, int) else 0


def list_sessions() -> int:
    """ls: the header row first (always), then one tab separated line per
    live session; stale dirs removed."""
    sys.stdout.write("\t".join(LS_COLUMNS) + "\n")
    root = sessions_root()
    if not root.is_dir():
        sys.stdout.flush()
        return EXIT_OK
    live: list[tuple[str, Path, dict[str, Any]]] = []
    for entry in sorted(root.iterdir()):
        if not entry.is_dir():
            continue
        meta = read_session_meta(entry)
        if meta is None:
            try:
                if time.time() - entry.stat().st_mtime < 10:
                    continue  # a daemon still writing its meta
            except OSError:
                continue
        session_id = meta.get("id") if meta is not None else None
        pid = meta.get("pid") if meta is not None else None
        if (
            not isinstance(session_id, str)
            or not isinstance(pid, int)
            or not pid_alive(pid)
        ):
            shutil.rmtree(entry, ignore_errors=True)
            continue
        live.append((session_id, entry, meta))
    for session_id, entry, meta in sorted(live, key=lambda row: row[0]):
        created = meta.get("created")
        age = (
            format_age(time.time() - created)
            if isinstance(created, (int, float))
            else "?"
        )
        caller = meta.get("caller")
        cwd = ""
        if isinstance(caller, dict) and isinstance(caller.get("cwd"), str):
            cwd = caller["cwd"]
        head = ""
        if isinstance(meta.get("message_head"), str):
            head = (
                meta["message_head"][:LIST_HEAD_CHARS]
                .replace("\n", " ")
                .replace("\r", " ")
            )
        who = meta.get("who") if isinstance(meta.get("who"), str) else ""
        if isinstance(meta.get("ended"), str):
            state = f"ended:{meta['ended']}, unread kept"
        else:
            state = f"open, idle ends in {query_idle_left(entry, meta)}s"
        sys.stdout.write(
            "\t".join(
                [
                    session_id,
                    str(meta["pid"]),
                    age,
                    state,
                    who,
                    cwd,
                    head,
                ]
            )
            + "\n"
        )
    sys.stdout.flush()
    return EXIT_OK


def close_session(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> int:
    """close ID: the daemon sends kind=close, drops the dir, exits."""
    conn = connect_session(session_dir, session_id, 0.0)
    if conn is None:
        eprint(f"no open session {session_id}")
        return EXIT_USAGE
    reason = END_LOCAL_CLOSE
    try:
        if send_event(conn, {"op": OP_CLOSE}):
            obj = read_json_line(conn, CTL_REPLY_TIMEOUT)
            if obj is not None and obj.get("ev") == "end":
                reason = str(obj.get("reason") or END_LOCAL_CLOSE)
    finally:
        close_quietly(conn)
    eprint(f"session {session_id} ended ({reason})")
    return EXIT_OK


def run_turn(
    session_dir: Path,
    session_id: str,
    message: Optional[str],
    wait_sec: int,
    connect_wait: float = 0.0,
    as_json: bool = False,
    bot_name: str = DEFAULT_BOT_NAME,
) -> int:
    """One background-session turn: send, stream the events, print the turn."""
    conn = connect_session(session_dir, session_id, connect_wait)
    if conn is None:
        eprint(f"no open session {session_id}")
        return EXIT_USAGE
    got_text = False
    got_relayed = False
    got_ack = False
    end_reason: Optional[str] = None
    close_reason: Optional[str] = None
    try:
        event: dict[str, Any] = {"op": OP_ATTACH}
        if message is not None:
            event = {"op": OP_MSG, "body": message + "\n"}
        if not send_event(conn, event):
            eprint(f"no open session {session_id}")
            return EXIT_USAGE
        # --wait counts from delivery: a line still being re-POSTed (retries
        # take up to ~40 s) must report its own outcome to this call.
        wait_deadline: Optional[float] = None
        if message is None:
            wait_deadline = time.monotonic() + wait_sec
        delivery_deadline = time.monotonic() + DELIVERY_WAIT_SEC
        settle_at: Optional[float] = None
        buf = bytearray()
        while end_reason is None and close_reason is None:
            limit = wait_deadline if wait_deadline is not None else delivery_deadline
            if settle_at is not None and settle_at < limit:
                limit = settle_at
            remaining = limit - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                break
            try:
                ready, _, _ = select.select([conn], [], [], remaining)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                break
            if not ready:
                break
            try:
                chunk = conn.recv(65536)
            except OSError:
                chunk = b""
            if not chunk:
                eprint(f"no open session {session_id}")
                return EXIT_USAGE
            buf.extend(chunk)
            for line in pop_json_lines(buf):
                try:
                    obj = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
                except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):
                    continue
                if not isinstance(obj, dict):
                    continue
                ev = obj.get("ev")
                if ev == "status":
                    body = obj.get("body")
                    if isinstance(body, str):
                        emit_status(body.encode("utf-8"))
                elif ev == "msg":
                    body = obj.get("body")
                    if isinstance(body, str):
                        from_name = obj.get("from")
                        if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                            from_name = None
                        queued_at = obj.get("queued_at")
                        if not isinstance(queued_at, str):
                            queued_at = None
                        try:
                            emit_stdout(
                                format_msg(from_name, body, queued_at).encode(
                                    "utf-8"
                                )
                            )
                        except BrokenPipeError:
                            eprint("stdout closed")
                            return EXIT_USAGE
                        got_text = True
                elif ev == "relayed":
                    name = obj.get("name")
                    if isinstance(name, str):
                        from_name = obj.get("from")
                        if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                            from_name = None
                        queued_at = obj.get("queued_at")
                        if not isinstance(queued_at, str):
                            queued_at = None
                        try:
                            emit_stdout(
                                format_relayed(from_name, name, queued_at).encode(
                                    "utf-8"
                                )
                            )
                        except BrokenPipeError:
                            pass
                        got_relayed = True
                elif ev == "ack":
                    from_name = obj.get("from")
                    if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                        from_name = None
                    try:
                        emit_stdout(format_ack(from_name).encode("utf-8"))
                    except BrokenPipeError:
                        eprint("stdout closed")
                        return EXIT_USAGE
                    got_ack = True
                elif ev == "close":
                    close_reason = str(obj.get("reason") or "")
                    break
                elif ev == "end":
                    end_reason = str(obj.get("reason") or "")
                    break
                elif ev in ("sent", "rewoke"):
                    eprint("sent")
                    if wait_deadline is None:
                        wait_deadline = time.monotonic() + wait_sec
                elif ev == "webhook_failed":
                    detail = obj.get("detail")
                    if not isinstance(detail, str) or not detail:
                        detail = "unknown error"
                    eprint(
                        f"could not reach {bot_name}: webhook failed ({detail}); "
                        "the line was not delivered and is not kept, resend "
                        "it yourself"
                    )
                    return EXIT_WEBHOOK
            if (
                end_reason is None
                and close_reason is None
                and (got_text or got_relayed or got_ack)
            ):
                settle_at = time.monotonic() + SETTLE_SEC
    finally:
        close_quietly(conn)
    if end_reason is None and close_reason is not None:
        end_reason = END_CLOSED
    if end_reason is None:
        if got_relayed:
            code = EXIT_RELAYED
        elif got_text:
            code = EXIT_OK
        elif got_ack:
            code = EXIT_ACKED
        else:
            code = EXIT_WAIT
            emit_stdout(
                f"# nothing yet (exit 8); wait {session_id} keeps waiting\n"
                .encode("utf-8")
            )
        emit_delivery(
            classify_delivery(got_relayed, got_ack, got_text), as_json
        )
        return code
    code = END_CODES.get(end_reason, EXIT_USAGE)
    if got_relayed and code == EXIT_OK:
        code = EXIT_RELAYED
    if (
        got_ack
        and not got_text
        and not got_relayed
        and code == EXIT_OK
    ):
        code = EXIT_ACKED
    eprint(f"session {session_id} ended ({end_reason})")
    if code != EXIT_WEBHOOK:
        emit_delivery(
            classify_delivery(got_relayed, got_ack, got_text), as_json
        )
    return code


def stop_old_daemon(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> None:
    """After a drain, wait for that daemon to go away and remove its dir.

    SIGTERM only while meta.json still names this session's live pid, so
    we never signal a pid the dir no longer owns.
    """
    pid = live_daemon_pid(session_dir, session_id)
    deadline = time.monotonic() + OLD_DAEMON_STOP_WAIT
    while pid is not None and time.monotonic() < deadline:
        time.sleep(PID_POLL_SEC)
        pid = live_daemon_pid(session_dir, session_id)
    if pid is None:
        return
    eprint(f"session {session_id} daemon pid {pid} did not stop; SIGTERM")
    try:
        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)
    except OSError:
        return
    deadline = time.monotonic() + OLD_DAEMON_STOP_WAIT
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        if live_daemon_pid(session_dir, session_id) is None:
            return
        time.sleep(PID_POLL_SEC)


def open_under_id(session_dir: Path, session_id: str) -> None:
    """Talk on an id that is not live: drain a lingering end, note old state.

    A lingering ended session is drained first (its unread frames go to
    stdout) so reopening the listener under the same id loses nothing. A
    brand-new id gets no note: there was no state here to replace.
    """
    state = session_state(session_dir, session_id)
    if state == STATE_ENDED:
        meta = read_session_meta(session_dir) or {}
        reason = meta.get("ended")
        if not isinstance(reason, str):
            reason = "?"
        eprint(
            f"session {session_id} had ended ({reason}); unread frames "
            "follow, then the listener reopens under the same id"
        )
        run_turn(session_dir, session_id, None, ENDED_DRAIN_WAIT_SEC)
        stop_old_daemon(session_dir, session_id)
    if state == STATE_ENDED or session_dir.exists():
        eprint(
            f"session {session_id} had prior state; reopening the listener "
            "under the same id"
        )


class _Parser(argparse.ArgumentParser):
    def error(self, message: str) -> None:  # type: ignore[override]
        eprint(message)
        eprint('try: asksoul -h')
        raise SystemExit(EXIT_USAGE)


def usage_fail(message: str) -> NoReturn:
    """The _Parser error style, for the checks argparse cannot do."""
    eprint(message)
    eprint('try: asksoul -h')
    raise SystemExit(EXIT_USAGE)


def print_version() -> NoReturn:
    """--version: like -h, before subcommand parsing; exits 0."""
    sys.stdout.write(f"asksoul {VERSION}\n")
    raise SystemExit(EXIT_OK)


def print_help(who_arg: Optional[str] = None) -> NoReturn:
    """Main help; -h, no args and a subcommand's -h all end here."""
    who, source, bot_name = peek_config()
    if who_arg is not None:
        try:
            who = _clean_ident(who_arg, "WHO", MAX_WHO_CHARS)
        except UsageError as exc:
            usage_fail(str(exc))
    sys.stdout.write(render_help(who, source, bot_name))
    raise SystemExit(EXIT_OK)


def check_session_id(session_id: str) -> None:
    """1..128 chars of A-Za-z0-9._:-, starting with a letter or digit."""
    if not SESSION_ID_RE.match(session_id):
        usage_fail(
            "session id must be 1..128 of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ : -, "
            "starting with a letter or digit"
        )


def parse_wait_sec(raw: Optional[str]) -> int:
    if raw is None:
        return DEFAULT_WAIT_SEC
    try:
        wait_sec = int(raw)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        usage_fail("--wait must be an integer number of seconds")
    if wait_sec < MIN_WAIT_SEC or wait_sec > MAX_WAIT_SEC:
        usage_fail(f"--wait must be {MIN_WAIT_SEC}..{MAX_WAIT_SEC}")
    return wait_sec


def parse_timeout_sec(raw: Optional[str]) -> int:
    if raw is None:
        return DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_SEC
    try:
        timeout_sec = int(raw)
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        usage_fail("-t must be an integer number of seconds")
    if timeout_sec < 1 or timeout_sec > MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC:
        usage_fail(f"-t must be 1..{MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC}")
    return timeout_sec


def new_parser() -> _Parser:
    """One parser shape for every command; usage is the main help's block."""
    return _Parser(
        prog="asksoul",
        add_help=False,
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
        usage=USAGE,
    )


def _toml_quote(text: str) -> str:
    return json.dumps(text, ensure_ascii=False)


def _prompt(text: str, default: str = "") -> str:
    suffix = f" [{default}]" if default else ""
    try:
        value = input(f"{text}{suffix}: ").strip()
    except EOFError:
        return default
    return value or default


def _prompt_secret() -> str:
    if sys.stdin.isatty():
        try:
            return getpass.getpass("Webhook secret: ").strip()
        except EOFError:
            return ""
    try:
        return sys.stdin.readline().strip()
    except EOFError:
        return ""


def _write_private(path: Path, text: str) -> None:
    """Write a file mode 0600, creating parent dirs mode 0700."""
    path.parent.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    try:
        os.chmod(path.parent, 0o700)
    except OSError:
        pass
    fd = os.open(str(path), os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as out:
            out.write(text)
    finally:
        try:
            os.chmod(path, 0o600)
        except OSError:
            pass


def parse_init(rest: list[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="asksoul init",
        description="Write ~/.config/asksoul/config.toml (mode 0600).",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--webhook-url", metavar="URL")
    parser.add_argument("--bot-name", metavar="NAME", default=None)
    secret_group = parser.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    secret_group.add_argument(
        "--secret-cmd", metavar="CMD", help="shell command that prints the secret"
    )
    secret_group.add_argument(
        "--secret-stdin",
        action="store_true",
        help="read the secret from stdin and write ~/.config/asksoul/secret",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--accept",
        action="append",
        default=[],
        metavar="HOST[,HOST...]",
        help="allowed dial-back IPs/hostnames (repeatable, comma separated)",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--accept-ssh-host", metavar="HOST", default=None)
    parser.add_argument("--who", metavar="WHO", default=None)
    parser.add_argument("--bind", metavar="IP", default=None)
    parser.add_argument(
        "--non-interactive",
        action="store_true",
        help="never prompt; missing required values are an error",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="overwrite an existing config")
    args = parser.parse_args(rest)
    return argparse.Namespace(cmd=CMD_INIT, **vars(args))


def cmd_init(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    path = config_path()
    interactive = not args.non_interactive and sys.stdin.isatty()
    if path.exists() and not args.force:
        if not interactive:
            eprint(f"{path} exists; use --force to overwrite")
            return EXIT_USAGE
        answer = _prompt(f"{path} exists; overwrite? [y/N]", "N")
        if answer.lower() not in ("y", "yes"):
            eprint("config kept")
            return EXIT_OK

    webhook_url = (args.webhook_url or "").strip()
    if not webhook_url:
        if not interactive:
            eprint("--webhook-url is required with --non-interactive")
            return EXIT_USAGE
        webhook_url = _prompt("Webhook URL")
    if not (webhook_url.startswith("https://") or webhook_url.startswith("http://")):
        eprint("webhook URL must start with http:// or https://")
        return EXIT_USAGE

    bot_name = (args.bot_name or "").strip()
    if not bot_name:
        if interactive:
            bot_name = _prompt("Bot name", DEFAULT_BOT_NAME)
        else:
            bot_name = DEFAULT_BOT_NAME
    try:
        bot_name = _clean_ident(bot_name, "bot_name", MAX_BOT_NAME_CHARS)
    except UsageError as exc:
        eprint(str(exc))
        return EXIT_USAGE

    accepts: list[str] = []
    for raw in args.accept:
        accepts.extend(part.strip() for part in raw.split(",") if part.strip())
    if interactive and not accepts:
        raw = _prompt(
            "Allowed dial-back IPs/hostnames (comma separated, blank to skip)"
        )
        accepts = [a.strip() for a in raw.split(",") if a.strip()]

    secret_cmd = (args.secret_cmd or "").strip()
    secret_text = ""
    if args.secret_stdin:
        secret_text = _prompt_secret()
        if not secret_text:
            eprint("--secret-stdin was given but stdin had no secret")
            return EXIT_USAGE
    elif not secret_cmd and interactive:
        choice = _prompt(
            "Webhook secret: [f]ile / [c]ommand / [s]kip (env later)", "f"
        ).lower()
        if choice.startswith("f"):
            secret_text = _prompt_secret()
            if not secret_text:
                eprint("empty secret; nothing written")
                return EXIT_USAGE
        elif choice.startswith("c"):
            secret_cmd = _prompt("Secret command")

    lines = [
        f"bot_name = {_toml_quote(bot_name)}",
        f"webhook_url = {_toml_quote(webhook_url)}",
    ]
    if args.who:
        lines.append(f"who = {_toml_quote(args.who.strip())}")
    if args.bind:
        lines.append(f"bind = {_toml_quote(args.bind.strip())}")
    if accepts:
        lines.append(
            "accept = ["
            + ", ".join(_toml_quote(a) for a in accepts)
            + "]"
        )
    if args.accept_ssh_host:
        lines.append(
            f"accept_ssh_host = {_toml_quote(args.accept_ssh_host.strip())}"
        )
    secret_path = path.parent / "secret"
    if secret_text:
        _write_private(secret_path, secret_text + "\n")
        lines.append(f"secret_file = {_toml_quote(str(secret_path))}")
    elif secret_cmd:
        lines.append(f"secret_cmd = {_toml_quote(secret_cmd)}")

    _write_private(path, "\n".join(lines) + "\n")
    eprint(f"wrote {path} (mode 0600)")
    if secret_text:
        eprint(f"wrote {secret_path} (mode 0600)")
    elif not secret_cmd:
        eprint(
            "no secret configured; set ASKSOUL_WEBHOOK_SECRET before using asksoul"
        )
    return EXIT_OK


def parse_subcommand(name: str, rest: list[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:
    """ls / close / wait / tui / init; argv[0] is one of them."""
    if name == CMD_INIT:
        return parse_init(rest)
    if "--version" in rest:
        print_version()
    if any(arg in ("-h", "--help") for arg in rest):
        print_help()
    parser = new_parser()
    if name == CMD_LS:
        parser.parse_args(rest)
        return argparse.Namespace(cmd=CMD_LS)
    if name == CMD_CLOSE:
        parser.add_argument("session_id", metavar="ID")
        args = parser.parse_args(rest)
        check_session_id(args.session_id)
        return argparse.Namespace(cmd=CMD_CLOSE, session_id=args.session_id)
    if name == CMD_TUI:
        parser.add_argument("-w", "--who", dest="who", metavar="WHO")
        parser.add_argument("-t", "--timeout", metavar="SEC")
        parser.add_argument("-s", "--session", metavar="ID")
        parser.add_argument("--wait", metavar="SEC")
        args = parser.parse_args(rest)
        if args.session is not None:
            check_session_id(args.session)
        who = None
        if args.who is not None:
            try:
                who = _clean_ident(args.who, "WHO", MAX_WHO_CHARS)
            except UsageError as exc:
                usage_fail(str(exc))
        return argparse.Namespace(
            cmd=CMD_TUI,
            session_id=(
                args.session
                if args.session is not None
                else str(uuid.uuid4())
            ),
            generated_id=args.session is None,
            who=who,
            who_given=args.who is not None,
            timeout_sec=parse_timeout_sec(args.timeout),
            timeout_given=args.timeout is not None,
            wait_sec=parse_wait_sec(args.wait),
        )
    parser.add_argument("session_id", metavar="ID")
    parser.add_argument("--wait", metavar="SEC")
    parser.add_argument("--json", dest="as_json", action="store_true")
    args = parser.parse_args(rest)
    check_session_id(args.session_id)
    return argparse.Namespace(
        cmd=CMD_WAIT,
        session_id=args.session_id,
        message=None,
        wait_sec=parse_wait_sec(args.wait),
        as_json=bool(args.as_json),
    )


def parse_args(argv: list[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:
    """Talk, notify and -s: one parser, then the cross-option rules."""
    if argv and argv[0] == "--version":
        print_version()
    if argv and argv[0] in SUBCOMMANDS:
        return parse_subcommand(argv[0], argv[1:])

    parser = new_parser()
    parser.add_argument("-h", "--help", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--version", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("-w", "--who", dest="who", metavar="WHO")
    parser.add_argument("-t", "--timeout", metavar="SEC")
    parser.add_argument("-s", "--session", metavar="ID")
    parser.add_argument("--wait", metavar="SEC")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--json",
        dest="as_json",
        action="store_true",
        help="also print delivery JSON after the DELIVERY line",
    )
    parser.add_argument("words", nargs="*", metavar="MESSAGE")

    # Intermixed: a positional word may follow an option
    # ("asksoul hi -w X there"), which plain parse_args() rejects.
    args = parser.parse_intermixed_args(argv)
    if args.version:
        print_version()
    if args.help or not argv:
        print_help(args.who)

    if args.session is not None:
        check_session_id(args.session)

    args.wait_sec = parse_wait_sec(args.wait)
    args.message = " ".join(args.words)
    if not args.words:
        if args.session is not None:
            usage_fail(
                "-s needs a message; to wait without sending use: asksoul wait ID"
            )
        usage_fail("a message is required")
    if args.message == "":
        usage_fail("message is empty")

    if args.who is not None:
        try:
            args.who = _clean_ident(args.who, "WHO", MAX_WHO_CHARS)
        except UsageError as exc:
            usage_fail(str(exc))

    # The session_id field is never optional in the data: -s names the
    # thread; without -s a fresh UUID is generated here and main prints it.
    args.generated_id = args.session is None
    args.session_id = (
        args.session if args.session is not None else str(uuid.uuid4())
    )

    # -w/-t apply only when this call opens the session (checked at run
    # time, when the session is known to be live or not).
    args.cmd = CMD_SESSION if args.session is not None else CMD_DEFAULT
    args.timeout_sec = parse_timeout_sec(args.timeout)
    args.as_json = bool(getattr(args, "as_json", False))
    return args


def open_session_now(
    session_dir: Path,
    session_id: str,
    message: str,
    who_override: Optional[str],
    timeout_sec: int,
    generated_id: bool,
    sender_type: str = "user-cli",
) -> int:
    """Open a new session for MESSAGE: bind, webhook, spawn the daemon.

    The CLI and the TUI both use this. It returns EXIT_OK once the
    background session is live and a caller may attach; otherwise the
    CLI error code (details already on stderr). The message is delivered
    by the webhook, exactly like a normal ask; it is not sent again over
    the control socket. TUI passes sender_type="user-tui" (continuous
    conversation: do not close after each answer).
    """
    open_under_id(session_dir, session_id)
    no_webhook = os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_NO_WEBHOOK") == "1"
    try:
        cfg = load_runtime_config(require_webhook=not no_webhook)
    except UsageError as exc:
        eprint(str(exc))
        return EXIT_USAGE
    except OSError:
        eprint("cannot read config")
        return EXIT_USAGE
    url = cfg["url"]
    sender_key = cfg["secret"]
    who = cfg["who"]
    source = cfg["source"]
    if who_override is not None:
        who = who_override

    if generated_id:
        # The id is ours for this run; the caller continues with -s.
        eprint(f"session {session_id} (continue with -s {session_id})")

    listener: Optional[socket.socket] = None
    key: Optional[bytes] = None
    try:
        try:
            host = self_bind_ipv4(cfg["data"])
            allow = accept_list(cfg["data"])
            key = make_key()
            listener, port = bind_listener(host)
        except SetupError as exc:
            eprint(str(exc))
            return EXIT_SETUP
        if live_session(session_dir, session_id) is not None:
            # Two callers opened this id at once: the other one opened
            # it while we were binding. Failing is the simple safe
            # choice: never clobber the session that won.
            eprint(f"session {session_id} is already open")
            return EXIT_USAGE
        shutil.rmtree(session_dir, ignore_errors=True)
        reply_meta = reply_object(host, port, timeout_sec, key, who)
        allow_note = ",".join(sorted(allow))
        sid = f" session={session_id}"
        fp = hashlib.sha256(key).hexdigest()[:8]
        eprint(
            f"listening {host}:{port} allow {allow_note} "
            f"idle timeout {timeout_sec}s{sid} key_fp={fp}"
        )

        payload = build_payload(
            message,
            reply_meta,
            session_id,
            source,
            who,
            sender_type=sender_type,
        )
        try:
            if os.environ.get("ASKSOUL_NO_WEBHOOK") == "1":
                line = json.dumps({"no_webhook": True,
                    "host": reply_meta["host"], "port": reply_meta["port"],
                    "key_b64": reply_meta["crypto"]["key_b64"],
                    "session_id": session_id})
                sys.stderr.write(line + "\n")
                sys.stderr.flush()
            else:
                post_webhook(url, sender_key, payload)
        except WebhookError as exc:
            eprint(f"webhook failed ({exc.detail})")
            return EXIT_WEBHOOK

        assert listener is not None and key is not None
        meta = build_session_meta(
            session_id,
            who,
            source,
            reply_meta["host"],
            reply_meta["port"],
            timeout_sec,
            message,
        )
        try:
            spawn_daemon(
                session_dir,
                meta,
                listener,
                key,
                allow,
                timeout_sec,
                session_id,
                who,
                source,
                reply_meta,
                url,
                sender_key,
            )
        except OSError:
            eprint("cannot start the background session process")
            return EXIT_SETUP
        # Plain close: the daemon owns the listener now, and shutdown()
        # would tear down the shared socket it is accepting on.
        try:
            listener.close()
        except OSError:
            pass
        listener = None
        return EXIT_OK
    finally:
        if listener is not None:
            close_quietly(listener)
        key = None


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TUI (asksoul tui): a small curses chat over the same session daemon.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


def _char_cells(ch: str) -> int:
    """Approximate terminal cells for one character (CJK is two)."""
    if unicodedata.combining(ch):
        return 0
    if unicodedata.east_asian_width(ch) in ("W", "F"):
        return 2
    return 1


def _display_width(text: str) -> int:
    return sum(_char_cells(ch) for ch in text)


def _take_cells(text: str, width: int) -> tuple[str, int]:
    """The longest prefix of text that fits in width cells (>= 1 char)."""
    used = 0
    for index, ch in enumerate(text):
        cells = _char_cells(ch)
        if used + cells > width and index > 0:
            return text[:index], used
        used += cells
    return text, used


def _clip_cells(text: str, width: int) -> str:
    """text cut to at most width cells (never splits a double-width char)."""
    if width <= 0:
        return ""
    if _display_width(text) <= width:
        return text
    head, _ = _take_cells(text, width)
    return head


_WORD_RE = re.compile(r"\s+|[^\s]+")


def wrap_display(text: str, width: int) -> list[str]:
    """Wrap text to width terminal cells; newlines are hard breaks.

    Long unbroken words (and CJK runs) are split by cells, so a line
    never exceeds the visible width.
    """
    width = max(1, width)
    out: list[str] = []
    for raw in text.replace("\t", "    ").split("\n"):
        raw = "".join(ch for ch in raw if ch.isprintable() or ch == " ")
        if raw == "":
            out.append("")
            continue
        line = ""
        line_w = 0
        for token in _WORD_RE.findall(raw):
            if token.isspace():
                if not line:
                    continue
                tw = _display_width(token)
                if line_w + tw <= width:
                    line += token
                    line_w += tw
                else:
                    out.append(line.rstrip())
                    line, line_w = "", 0
                continue
            tw = _display_width(token)
            if line_w + tw <= width:
                line += token
                line_w += tw
                continue
            if line:
                out.append(line.rstrip())
                line, line_w = "", 0
            while tw > width:
                head, used = _take_cells(token, width)
                if not head:
                    break
                out.append(head)
                token = token[len(head):]
                tw -= used
            if token:
                line, line_w = token, tw
        out.append(line.rstrip())
    return out


class _TuiTextCapture:
    """A sys.stdout/sys.stderr stand-in that keeps text (and .buffer)."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self._parts: list[str] = []
        self.buffer = self

    def write(self, data: Any) -> int:
        if isinstance(data, bytes):
            self._parts.append(data.decode("utf-8", "replace"))
        else:
            self._parts.append(str(data))
        return len(data)

    def flush(self) -> None:
        pass

    def getvalue(self) -> str:
        return "".join(self._parts)


class Tui:
    """The curses UI. One thread only; the open path uses a worker thread."""

    def __init__(self, stdscr: Any, args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:
        self.scr = stdscr
        self.session_id: str = args.session_id
        self.generated_id: bool = args.generated_id
        self.session_dir = session_dir_for(self.session_id)
        self.who_override: Optional[str] = args.who
        self.timeout_sec: int = args.timeout_sec
        self.wait_sec: int = args.wait_sec
        help_who, _help_source, self.bot_name = peek_config()
        self.who: str = args.who if args.who is not None else help_who
        self.transcript: deque[tuple[str, int]] = deque(
            maxlen=TUI_MAX_ENTRIES
        )
        self.version = 0
        self.wrap_cache_width: Optional[int] = None
        self.wrap_cache_version = -1
        self.wrap_cache: list[tuple[str, int]] = []
        self.scroll_from_bottom = 0
        self.draft = ""
        self.phase = "idle"  # idle | opening | waiting
        self.wait_started = 0.0
        self.wait_deadline: Optional[float] = None
        self.wait_kind = ""
        self.session_open = False
        self.ctl: Optional[socket.socket] = None
        self.ctl_buf = bytearray()
        self.open_queue: Optional[queue.Queue] = None
        self.open_in_flight = False
        self.open_cancelled = False
        self.idle_left: Optional[int] = None
        self.info_at: Optional[float] = None
        self.last_info_request = 0.0
        self._last_draw_sec = -1
        self.running = True
        self.dirty = True
        self.exit_code = EXIT_OK
        self.pasting = False

    # -- transcript -----------------------------------------------------

    def add_text(self, text: str, style: int = 0) -> None:
        if text == "":
            return
        self.transcript.append((text, style))
        self.version += 1
        self.dirty = True

    def add_system(self, text: str) -> None:
        self.add_text(text, curses.A_DIM)

    # -- lifecycle ------------------------------------------------------

    def run(self) -> int:
        try:
            curses.raw()
        except curses.error:
            pass
        try:
            curses.curs_set(1)
        except curses.error:
            pass
        self.scr.keypad(True)
        self.scr.timeout(TUI_TICK_MS)
        self._set_bracketed_paste(True)
        self.add_system(
            f"# asksoul tui {VERSION} — session {self.session_id}"
        )
        self.add_system("# /help for commands; first Enter opens the session")
        self.attach_existing()
        try:
            while self.running:
                self.drain_open_result()
                self.read_ctl()
                self.tick()
                self.draw()
                self.handle_key(self.get_key())
        finally:
            self._set_bracketed_paste(False)
            self.close_ctl()
        return self.exit_code

    def _set_bracketed_paste(self, on: bool) -> None:
        """Ask the terminal to wrap pastes in CSI 200~/201~ (DECSET 2004)."""
        seq = TUI_BRACKETED_PASTE_ON if on else TUI_BRACKETED_PASTE_OFF
        for fd in (sys.stdout.fileno(), sys.stderr.fileno()):
            try:
                os.write(fd, seq)
                return
            except OSError:
                continue

    def _read_csi_after_esc(self) -> str:
        """Drain a CSI after a bare Esc; restore get_wch timeout afterward.

        Returns the CSI body including '[' and the final byte (e.g. '[200~'),
        or '' if nothing followed (bare Esc / timeout).
        """
        self.scr.timeout(TUI_ESC_PEEK_MS)
        try:
            try:
                ch = self.scr.get_wch()
            except curses.error:
                return ""
            if ch != "[" and ch != ord("["):
                # Not CSI: push the key back if possible, else drop.
                try:
                    if isinstance(ch, str):
                        curses.unget_wch(ch)
                    else:
                        curses.ungetch(ch)
                except (curses.error, TypeError, OverflowError):
                    pass
                return ""
            parts = ["["]
            while True:
                try:
                    nxt = self.scr.get_wch()
                except curses.error:
                    break
                if isinstance(nxt, int):
                    # Unexpected keypad code mid-CSI; stop.
                    try:
                        curses.ungetch(nxt)
                    except (curses.error, OverflowError):
                        pass
                    break
                parts.append(nxt)
                # CSI final byte is in @-_ or ~ for the paste markers.
                if ("@" <= nxt <= "~") and nxt not in "0123456789;?:":
                    break
                if len(parts) > 16:
                    break
            return "".join(parts)
        finally:
            self.scr.timeout(TUI_TICK_MS)

    def close_ctl(self) -> None:
        if self.ctl is not None:
            close_quietly(self.ctl)
            self.ctl = None
        self.ctl_buf.clear()
        self.session_open = False

    def attach_existing(self) -> None:
        """With -s, attach a live session (inbound frames show immediately)."""
        if self.generated_id:
            return
        state = session_state(self.session_dir, self.session_id)
        if state == STATE_LIVE:
            if self.attach_ctl(TUI_ATTACH_WAIT_SEC):
                self.add_system(f"# attached to session {self.session_id}")
            else:
                self.add_system(
                    f"# session {self.session_id} is open but did not "
                    "answer; first Enter opens a new one"
                )
        elif state == STATE_ENDED:
            meta = read_session_meta(self.session_dir) or {}
            reason = meta.get("ended")
            if not isinstance(reason, str):
                reason = "?"
            self.add_system(
                f"# session {self.session_id} ended ({reason}); "
                "first Enter opens a new one"
            )
        else:
            self.add_system(
                f"# no open session {self.session_id}; "
                "first Enter opens a new one"
            )

    def attach_ctl(self, wait: float) -> bool:
        conn = connect_session(self.session_dir, self.session_id, wait)
        if conn is None:
            return False
        if not send_event(conn, {"op": OP_ATTACH}):
            close_quietly(conn)
            return False
        self.ctl = conn
        self.session_open = True
        self.last_info_request = 0.0
        return True

    # -- opening (worker thread: the webhook POST can take ~40 s) -------

    def start_open(self, text: str) -> None:
        self.phase = "opening"
        self.open_in_flight = True
        self.open_cancelled = False
        self.wait_started = time.monotonic()
        self.wait_deadline = None
        self.wait_kind = "open"
        self.open_queue = queue.Queue()
        session_dir = self.session_dir
        session_id = self.session_id
        who_override = self.who_override
        timeout_sec = self.timeout_sec
        result_q = self.open_queue

        def work() -> None:
            out_cap = _TuiTextCapture()
            err_cap = _TuiTextCapture()
            code = EXIT_SETUP
            try:
                with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out_cap):
                    with contextlib.redirect_stderr(err_cap):
                        code = open_session_now(
                            session_dir,
                            session_id,
                            text,
                            who_override,
                            timeout_sec,
                            False,
                            sender_type="user-tui",
                        )
            except BaseException as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 - reported in pane
                err_cap.write(f"asksoul: opening failed: {exc}\n")
                code = EXIT_SETUP
            result_q.put((code, out_cap.getvalue(), err_cap.getvalue()))

        threading.Thread(
            target=work, name="asksoul-tui-open", daemon=True
        ).start()
        self.dirty = True

    def drain_open_result(self) -> None:
        if self.open_queue is None:
            return
        try:
            code, out_text, err_text = self.open_queue.get_nowait()
        except queue.Empty:
            return
        self.open_queue = None
        self.open_in_flight = False
        for line in err_text.splitlines():
            if not line.strip():
                continue
            if "key_b64" in line or "WEBHOOK_SENDER_KEY" in line:
                continue  # never put a secret in the pane
            if line.startswith("asksoul: "):
                line = line[len("asksoul: "):]
            self.add_system(f"# {line}")
        for line in out_text.splitlines():
            # A lingering ended session's unread frames (CLI format).
            if line.strip():
                style = curses.A_DIM if line.startswith("#") else 0
                self.add_text(line, style)
        self.phase = "idle"
        self.wait_deadline = None
        self.wait_kind = ""
        if code != EXIT_OK:
            self.add_system(
                f"# error: could not open the session (exit {code})"
            )
            self.dirty = True
            return
        if self.attach_ctl(TUI_ATTACH_WAIT_SEC):
            self.add_system(f"# session open; waiting for {self.bot_name}")
            if not self.open_cancelled:
                # The first line went out with the webhook: it is a turn too.
                self.start_wait("send")
        else:
            self.add_system(
                "# error: session opened but the control socket did not answer"
            )
        self.dirty = True

    # -- sending --------------------------------------------------------

    def send_msg(self, text: str) -> bool:
        if self.ctl is None:
            return False
        ok = send_event(self.ctl, {"op": OP_MSG, "body": text + "\n"})
        if not ok:
            self.close_ctl()
        return ok

    def submit(self) -> None:
        text = self.draft
        if not text.strip():
            self.draft = ""
            self.dirty = True
            return
        if text.startswith("/"):
            self.draft = ""
            self.dirty = True
            self.slash(text.strip())
            return
        if self.open_in_flight:
            self.add_system(
                "# still opening the session; the line was not sent"
            )
            return
        self.draft = ""
        self.dirty = True
        self.add_text(f"[you] {text}")
        if not self.session_open:
            self.start_open(text)
            return
        if not self.send_msg(text):
            self.add_system(
                "# error: the session is not reachable; "
                "reopening under the same session id"
            )
            self.start_open(text)
            return
        self.start_wait("send")

    def slash(self, text: str) -> None:
        if text == "/help":
            for line in TUI_HELP_LINES:
                self.add_system(line)
            return
        if text == "/clear":
            self.transcript.clear()
            self.version += 1
            self.scroll_from_bottom = 0
            self.dirty = True
            return
        if text == "/wait":
            if not self.session_open:
                self.add_system(
                    "# no open session; type a message and press Enter first"
                )
                return
            self.add_system("# waiting for the next inbound message")
            self.start_wait("cmd")
            return
        if text in ("/close", "/quit"):
            self.quit_tui()
            return
        self.add_system(f"# unknown command: {text} (try /help)")

    # -- wait/status ----------------------------------------------------

    def start_wait(self, kind: str) -> None:
        self.phase = "waiting"
        self.wait_kind = kind
        self.wait_started = time.monotonic()
        self.wait_deadline = self.wait_started + self.wait_sec
        self.dirty = True

    def end_wait(self) -> None:
        if self.phase == "waiting":
            self.phase = "idle"
            self.wait_deadline = None
            self.wait_kind = ""
            self.dirty = True

    def tick(self) -> None:
        now = time.monotonic()
        if (
            self.phase == "waiting"
            and self.wait_deadline is not None
            and now >= self.wait_deadline
        ):
            self.phase = "idle"
            self.wait_deadline = None
            self.wait_kind = ""
            self.add_system("# nothing yet (still listening)")
        if (
            self.ctl is not None
            and now - self.last_info_request >= TUI_INFO_POLL_SEC
        ):
            self.last_info_request = now
            if not send_event(self.ctl, {"op": OP_INFO}):
                self.on_disconnect()

    def quit_tui(self) -> None:
        if self.ctl is not None:
            try:
                if send_event(self.ctl, {"op": OP_CLOSE}):
                    read_json_line(self.ctl, 1.0)
            except OSError:
                pass
        self.close_ctl()
        self.phase = "idle"
        self.wait_deadline = None
        self.running = False

    def on_disconnect(self) -> None:
        was_open = self.session_open
        self.close_ctl()
        if self.phase == "waiting":
            self.phase = "idle"
            self.wait_deadline = None
            self.wait_kind = ""
        if was_open:
            self.add_system("# session disconnected")

    # -- control socket -------------------------------------------------

    def read_ctl(self) -> None:
        if self.ctl is None:
            return
        # An event handler (close/end) may close the socket mid-batch.
        while self.ctl is not None:
            try:
                ready, _, _ = select.select([self.ctl], [], [], 0)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                self.on_disconnect()
                return
            if not ready:
                return
            try:
                chunk = self.ctl.recv(65536)
            except OSError:
                chunk = b""
            if not chunk:
                self.on_disconnect()
                return
            self.ctl_buf.extend(chunk)
            while True:
                nl = self.ctl_buf.find(b"\n")
                if nl == -1:
                    break
                line = bytes(self.ctl_buf[:nl])
                del self.ctl_buf[: nl + 1]
                if line.endswith(b"\r"):
                    line = line[:-1]
                if not line.strip():
                    continue
                try:
                    obj = json.loads(line.decode("utf-8"))
                except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError):
                    continue
                if isinstance(obj, dict):
                    self.on_event(obj)
            if len(self.ctl_buf) > MAX_FRAME_BYTES:
                self.ctl_buf.clear()

    def _refresh_info(self) -> None:
        self.idle_left = None
        self.info_at = None
        self.last_info_request = 0.0

    def on_event(self, obj: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
        ev = obj.get("ev")
        if ev == "info":
            left = obj.get("idle_left")
            if isinstance(left, (int, float)):
                self.idle_left = max(0, int(left))
                self.info_at = time.monotonic()
            timeout = obj.get("timeout_sec")
            if isinstance(timeout, int):
                self.timeout_sec = timeout
            who = obj.get("who")
            if isinstance(who, str) and who:
                self.who = who
            ended = obj.get("ended")
            if isinstance(ended, str):
                self.add_system(f"# session ended ({ended})")
                self.end_wait()
                self.close_ctl()
            self.dirty = True
        elif ev == "status":
            body = obj.get("body")
            if isinstance(body, str):
                self.add_system(f"# status: {body.rstrip(chr(10))}")
            self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "msg":
            body = obj.get("body")
            if isinstance(body, str):
                from_name = obj.get("from")
                if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                    from_name = None
                queued_at = obj.get("queued_at")
                if not isinstance(queued_at, str):
                    queued_at = None
                text = format_msg(from_name, body, queued_at)
                if text.endswith("\n"):
                    text = text[:-1]
                self.add_text(text)
                self.end_wait()
                self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "relayed":
            name = obj.get("name")
            if isinstance(name, str):
                from_name = obj.get("from")
                if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                    from_name = None
                queued_at = obj.get("queued_at")
                if not isinstance(queued_at, str):
                    queued_at = None
                self.add_text(
                    format_relayed(from_name, name, queued_at).rstrip("\n"),
                    curses.A_DIM,
                )
                self.end_wait()
                self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "ack":
            from_name = obj.get("from")
            if not isinstance(from_name, str):
                from_name = None
            self.add_text(
                format_ack(from_name).rstrip("\n"), curses.A_DIM
            )
            self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "close":
            reason = obj.get("reason")
            reason = reason if isinstance(reason, str) else ""
            note = "# session closed" + (f" ({reason})" if reason else "")
            self.add_system(note)
            self.add_system(
                f"# same session id {self.session_id}; next Enter reopens it"
            )
            self.end_wait()
            self.close_ctl()
        elif ev == "end":
            reason = obj.get("reason")
            reason = reason if isinstance(reason, str) else ""
            note = "# session ended" + (f" ({reason})" if reason else "")
            self.add_system(note)
            self.add_system(
                f"# same session id {self.session_id}; next Enter reopens it"
            )
            self.end_wait()
            self.close_ctl()
        elif ev == "sent":
            self.add_system("# status: sent")
            self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "rewoke":
            self.add_system(f"# status: webhook re-sent; waiting for {self.bot_name}")
            self._refresh_info()
        elif ev == "webhook_failed":
            detail = obj.get("detail")
            if not isinstance(detail, str) or not detail:
                detail = "unknown error"
            self.add_system(
                f"# error: could not reach {self.bot_name}; the line was not delivered "
                f"({detail})"
            )
            self.end_wait()

    # -- keys -----------------------------------------------------------

    def get_key(self) -> Any:
        try:
            return self.scr.get_wch()
        except curses.error:
            return None

    def on_ctrl_c(self) -> None:
        if self.phase in ("waiting", "opening"):
            if self.phase == "opening":
                self.open_cancelled = True
            self.phase = "idle"
            self.wait_deadline = None
            self.wait_kind = ""
            self.add_system("# cancelled")
            return
        self.quit_tui()

    def handle_key(self, key: Any) -> None:
        if key is None:
            return
        if isinstance(key, str):
            if key == "\x03":
                self.on_ctrl_c()
            elif key in ("\n", "\r"):
                if self.pasting:
                    self.draft += "\n"
                    self.dirty = True
                else:
                    self.submit()
            elif key in ("\x7f", "\x08"):
                if self.draft:
                    self.draft = self.draft[:-1]
                    self.dirty = True
            elif key == "\x1b":
                csi = self._read_csi_after_esc()
                if csi == TUI_PASTE_BEGIN:
                    self.pasting = True
                elif csi == TUI_PASTE_END:
                    self.pasting = False
                elif csi == "":
                    # Bare Esc: clear draft (unchanged).
                    if self.draft:
                        self.draft = ""
                        self.dirty = True
                # Unknown CSI: ignore (do not clear draft mid-sequence).
            elif key == "\x0c":
                try:
                    self.scr.clear()
                except curses.error:
                    pass
                self.dirty = True
            elif key == "\t":
                if self.pasting:
                    self.draft += "\t"
                    self.dirty = True
            elif key.isprintable():
                self.draft += key
                self.dirty = True
            return
        if key == curses.KEY_RESIZE:
            try:
                self.scr.clear()
            except curses.error:
                pass
            self.dirty = True
        elif key == curses.KEY_PPAGE:
            self.scroll_page(1)
        elif key == curses.KEY_NPAGE:
            self.scroll_page(-1)
        elif key == curses.KEY_UP:
            self.scroll_lines(1)
        elif key == curses.KEY_DOWN:
            self.scroll_lines(-1)
        elif key == curses.KEY_BACKSPACE:
            if self.draft:
                self.draft = self.draft[:-1]
                self.dirty = True
        elif key == curses.KEY_ENTER:
            if self.pasting:
                self.draft += "\n"
                self.dirty = True
            else:
                self.submit()
        elif key == curses.KEY_DC:
            pass

    def scroll_page(self, direction: int) -> None:
        height, _ = self.scr.getmaxyx()
        page = max(
            1, height - 1 - TUI_INPUT_MAX_ROWS - TUI_SCROLL_PAGE_MARGIN
        )
        self.scroll_from_bottom = max(
            0, self.scroll_from_bottom + direction * page
        )
        self.dirty = True

    def scroll_lines(self, direction: int) -> None:
        self.scroll_from_bottom = max(
            0, self.scroll_from_bottom + direction
        )
        self.dirty = True

    # -- drawing --------------------------------------------------------

    def _flat_lines(self, width: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:
        if (
            self.wrap_cache_width == width
            and self.wrap_cache_version == self.version
        ):
            return self.wrap_cache
        flat: list[tuple[str, int]] = []
        for text, style in self.transcript:
            for line in wrap_display(text, width):
                flat.append((line, style))
        self.wrap_cache_width = width
        self.wrap_cache_version = self.version
        self.wrap_cache = flat
        return flat

    def _addstr(
        self, row: int, col: int, text: str, style: int = 0
    ) -> None:
        try:
            self.scr.addstr(row, col, text, style)
        except curses.error:
            pass

    def draw(self) -> None:
        now = time.monotonic()
        sec = int(now)
        needs = self.dirty
        if self.phase != "idle" and sec != self._last_draw_sec:
            needs = True
        if not needs:
            return
        self.dirty = False
        self._last_draw_sec = sec
        try:
            height, width = self.scr.getmaxyx()
        except curses.error:
            return
        if height < 1 or width < 1:
            return
        width = max(1, width)

        idle_text = "—"
        if self.idle_left is not None and self.info_at is not None:
            idle_text = (
                f"{max(0, self.idle_left - int(now - self.info_at))}s"
            )
        parts = [
            "asksoul tui",
            f"session: {self.session_id}",
            f"who: {self.who}",
            f"idle: {idle_text}",
        ]
        if self.phase == "opening":
            parts.append(f"opening… {int(now - self.wait_started)}s")
        elif self.phase == "waiting":
            parts.append(f"waiting… {int(now - self.wait_started)}s")
        status = "   ".join(parts)
        # Pad under A_REVERSE so a shorter status does not leave old cells.
        status_cells = _clip_cells(status, width - 1)
        pad = max(0, (width - 1) - _display_width(status_cells))
        self._addstr(0, 0, status_cells + (" " * pad), curses.A_REVERSE)

        avail = max(1, width - 2)
        wrapped = wrap_display(self.draft, avail)
        if not wrapped:
            wrapped = [""]
        if height <= 1:
            return
        input_h = min(
            max(1, len(wrapped)), TUI_INPUT_MAX_ROWS, height - 1
        )
        shown = wrapped[-input_h:]
        trans_h = max(0, height - 1 - input_h)
        if trans_h > 0:
            flat = self._flat_lines(width)
            max_offset = max(0, len(flat) - trans_h)
            self.scroll_from_bottom = min(
                self.scroll_from_bottom, max_offset
            )
            start = max(
                0, len(flat) - trans_h - self.scroll_from_bottom
            )
            visible = flat[start : start + trans_h]
            for row in range(trans_h):
                if row < len(visible):
                    text, style = visible[row]
                else:
                    text, style = "", 0
                self._addstr(1 + row, 0, text, style)
                try:
                    self.scr.clrtoeol()
                except curses.error:
                    pass

        input_top = height - input_h
        # When Backspace shrinks wrapped input rows, those rows move into
        # the transcript band (trans_h grows) and are redrawn + clrtoeol
        # above — no separate leftover wipe (that would erase transcript).
        first_prefix = "> " if len(wrapped) <= len(shown) else "  "
        for row, line in enumerate(shown):
            prefix = first_prefix if row == 0 else "  "
            self._addstr(input_top + row, 0, prefix + line)
            # Backspace / Esc shorten the draft; without clrtoeol the old
            # glyphs stay on screen (classic curses leftover).
            try:
                self.scr.clrtoeol()
            except curses.error:
                pass
        cursor_row = input_top + len(shown) - 1
        cursor_col = 2 + _display_width(shown[-1])
        cursor_col = max(0, min(cursor_col, width - 1))
        try:
            self.scr.move(cursor_row, cursor_col)
        except curses.error:
            pass


def run_tui(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:
    """Entry for `asksoul tui`; returns the process exit code."""
    if not (sys.stdin.isatty() and sys.stdout.isatty()):
        sys.stderr.write("asksoul tui needs a TTY\n")
        try:
            sys.stderr.flush()
        except OSError:
            pass
        return EXIT_WEBHOOK  # SPEC: exit 2 when not a TTY.
    if not args.generated_id:
        state = session_state(
            session_dir_for(args.session_id), args.session_id
        )
        if state == STATE_LIVE and (
            args.who_given or args.timeout_given
        ):
            eprint(
                f"session {args.session_id} is open; -w and -t only apply "
                "when a session opens"
            )
            return EXIT_USAGE
    if args.generated_id:
        eprint(f"session {args.session_id}")
    try:
        locale.setlocale(locale.LC_ALL, "")
    except locale.Error:
        pass
    os.environ.setdefault("ESCDELAY", "25")

    def _tui_stop(signum: int, frame: Any) -> None:
        raise KeyboardInterrupt

    old_handlers: dict[int, Any] = {}
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
        try:
            old_handlers[sig] = signal.signal(sig, _tui_stop)
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
    try:
        return int(curses.wrapper(lambda scr: Tui(scr, args).run()))
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        return EXIT_OK
    except curses.error as exc:
        eprint(f"tui: curses error: {exc}")
        return EXIT_SETUP
    finally:
        for sig, handler in old_handlers.items():
            try:
                signal.signal(sig, handler)
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                pass


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    if os.environ.get(DAEMON_FD_ENV):
        # Not a CLI call: this process is the exec'd background session
        # (spawn_daemon set the marker; see daemon_entry).
        return daemon_entry()
    try:
        args = parse_args(argv)
    except SystemExit as exc:
        code = exc.code
        if code is None:
            return EXIT_OK
        return int(code) if isinstance(code, int) else EXIT_USAGE

    try:
        if args.cmd == CMD_INIT:
            return cmd_init(args)
        if args.cmd == CMD_LS:
            return list_sessions()
        if args.cmd == CMD_CLOSE:
            return close_session(session_dir_for(args.session_id), args.session_id)
        _, _, bot_name = peek_config()
        if args.cmd == CMD_WAIT:
            return run_turn(
                session_dir_for(args.session_id),
                args.session_id,
                None,
                args.wait_sec,
                as_json=getattr(args, "as_json", False),
                bot_name=bot_name,
            )
        if args.cmd == CMD_TUI:
            return run_tui(args)
        # Talk: a live session under this id is continued. Anything else
        # (new, closed or expired) opens a new session under it: the -s
        # ID, or the UUID parse_args generated when -s was omitted.
        session_dir = session_dir_for(args.session_id)
        if session_state(session_dir, args.session_id) == STATE_LIVE:
            # Open and not ended: continue it. -w/-t apply only when a
            # call opens a session, so on an already open one they are a
            # usage error here, before anything is sent.
            if args.who is not None or args.timeout is not None:
                usage_fail(
                    f"session {args.session_id} is open; -w and -t only "
                    "apply when a session opens"
                )
            return run_turn(
                session_dir,
                args.session_id,
                args.message,
                args.wait_sec,
                as_json=getattr(args, "as_json", False),
                bot_name=bot_name,
            )
        # Not live: drain a lingering end, then open a new session.
        code = open_session_now(
            session_dir,
            args.session_id,
            args.message,
            args.who,
            args.timeout_sec,
            args.generated_id,
        )
        if code != EXIT_OK:
            return code
        return run_turn(
            session_dir,
            args.session_id,
            None,
            args.wait_sec,
            DAEMON_READY_TIMEOUT,
            as_json=getattr(args, "as_json", False),
            bot_name=bot_name,
        )
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        eprint("interrupted")
        return EXIT_USAGE


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
